(1342, 12, 'SCHEME OF EXAMINATION', 'Paper 1', 'will consist of forty multiple-choice objective questions all of which are to be answered in 1 hour for 40 marks. The paper will consist of two sections, Sections A and B as follows:', 'Paper 1, multiple choice, objective questions, 40 questions, 1 hour, 40 marks, Section A, Section B'),
(1343, 12, 'SCHEME OF EXAMINATION', 'Paper 1 - Section A', 'will consist of thirty questions drawn from the general principles, techniques and uses of plane and solid geometry.', 'Section A, plane geometry, solid geometry, general principles, techniques, 30 questions'),
(1344, 12, 'SCHEME OF EXAMINATION', 'Paper 1 - Section B', 'will consist of ten questions in each of two alternative parts: Part I (Building Drawing) and Part II (Mechanical Drawing). Candidates will be required to answer questions in one part only.', 'Section B, Part I, Building Drawing, Part II, Mechanical Drawing, 10 questions each, choose one part'),
(1345, 12, 'SCHEME OF EXAMINATION', 'Paper 2', 'will consist of five essay questions on plane, solid and vector geometry. Candidates will be required to answer any three of the questions in 1¼ hours for 60 marks.', 'Paper 2, essay questions, 5 questions, plane geometry, solid geometry, vector geometry, answer any three, 1¼ hours, 60 marks'),
(1346, 12, 'SCHEME OF EXAMINATION', 'Paper 3', 'will consist of two sections, Sections A and B to be taken in 2¼ hours for 100 marks.', 'Paper 3, Section A, Section B, 2¼ hours, 100 marks'),
(1347, 12, 'SCHEME OF EXAMINATION', 'Paper 3 - Section A', 'will consist of three questions requiring sketches of objects, components, symbols and tools used in the Building and Mechanical industries. One of the questions will be compulsory. Candidates will be required to answer the compulsory question for 20 marks and one of the other questions for 10 marks. The section will require 45 minutes.', 'Section A, sketches, objects, components, symbols, tools, Building industry, Mechanical industry, compulsory question, answer two, 20 marks, 10 marks, 45 minutes'),
(1348, 12, 'SCHEME OF EXAMINATION', 'Paper 3 - Section B', 'will consist of two questions: one on Building Drawing and the other, on Mechanical Drawing. Candidates will be required to answer only one of the questions in 2 hours for 70 marks.', 'Section B, Building Drawing, Mechanical Drawing, two questions, answer one, 2 hours, 70 marks'),
