(4882, 137, 'The theory of evolution can be defined as', 'The belief that all species were created in their current form', 'The hypothesis that organisms strive to improve themselves over generations', 'The idea that species change over time through natural processes', 'The concept that evolution occurs through a series of sudden and dramatic changes', 'C'),
(4883, 137, 'Which of the following is a male reproductive organ in humans?', 'Uterus', 'Ovary', 'Testis', 'Fallopian tube', 'C'),
(4884, 137, 'Which of the following is an example of a behavioral adaptation for survival in animals?', 'Sharp teeth', 'Migration', 'Wings', 'Camouflage', 'B'),
(4885, 137, 'Which of the following traits is not visible in a person with Down syndrome?', 'Short neck', 'High muscle tone', 'Small stature', 'Slant eyes', 'B'),
(4886, 137, 'What is the definition of population ecology?', 'The study of interactions between organisms and their physical environment', 'The study of evolutionary processes and their effects on populations', 'The study of interactions between different populations in an ecosystem', 'The study of the distribution and abundance of individuals within a species', 'D'),
(4887, 137, 'What is the term used to describe the maximum number of individuals of a species that an environment can support indefinitely?', 'Ecological niche', 'Limiting factor', 'Carrying capacity', 'Density-dependent factor', 'C'),
(4888, 137, 'Which of the following statements about the heart is true?', 'The heart is responsible for the production of red blood cells', 'The heart pumps oxygenated blood to the lungs', 'The heart receives blood from the kidneys and filters waste products', 'The heart is a muscular organ that contracts to circulate blood throughout the body', 'D'),
(4889, 137, 'What is the primary source of variation in a population?', 'Gene flow', 'Mutation', 'Natural selection', 'Genetic drift', 'B'),
(4890, 137, 'Which component of blood is responsible for carrying oxygen to the body tissues?', 'Platelets', 'White blood cells', 'Red blood cells', 'Plasma', 'C'),
(4891, 137, 'What are the primary products of photosynthesis?', 'Carbon dioxide and water', 'Glucose and oxygen', 'Glucose and carbon dioxide', 'Oxygen and water', 'B'),
(4892, 137, 'The alternate form of a gene is', 'Alternate type', 'Dominant character', 'Recessive character', 'Allele', 'D'),
(4893, 137, 'Which organs are part of the alimentary canal in the human digestive system?', 'Salivary glands, tongue, and pharynx', 'Large intestine, appendix, and rectum', 'Stomach, liver, and gallbladder', 'Oesophagus, pancreas, and small intestine', 'B'),
(4894, 137, 'Which of the following characteristics is typical of the phylum Arthropoda?', 'Radial symmetry', 'Closed circulatory system', 'Endoskeleton made of bones', 'Presence of a segmented body', 'D'),
(4895, 137, 'Which of the following is an example of conserving resources in an ecosystem?', 'Excessive use of chemical fertilizers in agriculture', 'Introducing invasive species to an ecosystem', 'Implementing sustainable fishing practices', 'Cutting down trees for timber production', 'C'),
(4896, 137, 'Which of the following represents the correct hierarchical organization of life from the smallest to the largest scale?', 'Organs, tissues, cells, organisms, populations, communities, ecosystems', 'Cells, organs, tissues, organisms, populations, communities, ecosystems', 'Tissues, organs, cells, organisms, populations, communities, ecosystems', 'Cells, tissues, organs, organisms, populations, communities, ecosystems', 'D'),
(4897, 137, 'Which of the following blood vessels carries oxygenated blood away from the heart?', 'Arteries', 'Venules', 'Capillaries', 'Veins', 'A'),
(4898, 137, 'Which of the following factors primarily affects the distribution of organisms in an ecosystem?', 'Wind speed', 'Soil pH', 'Temperature', 'Day length', 'C'),
(4899, 137, 'Which of the following is NOT a method of reproduction in animals?', 'Asexual reproduction', 'Budding', 'Sexual reproduction', 'Sporulation', 'D'),
(4900, 137, 'Which of the following statements is true about the kingdom Fungi?', 'Fungi obtain nutrients by absorbing organic matter', 'Fungi are photosynthetic organisms', 'Fungi are multicellular organisms', 'Fungi reproduce through the formation of seeds', 'A'),
(4901, 137, 'Viviparity refers to the reproductive strategy in which', 'Offspring are produced by internal fertilization', 'Offspring are produced by external fertilization', 'Offspring develop and are nourished inside the female\'s body', 'Offspring develop and are nourished outside the female\'s body', 'C'),
(4902, 137, 'Which of the following is the most inclusive level of classification in the Linnaean system?', 'Kingdom', 'Phylum', 'Domain', 'Class', 'C'),
(4903, 137, 'Which of the following describes the inheritance of traits from parents to offspring?', 'Adaptation', 'Evolution', 'Natural selection', 'Genetics', 'D'),
(4904, 137, 'Which of the following statements best describes the role of competition in the process of adaptation?', 'Competition leads to the selection of individuals with favorable traits for survival and reproduction', 'Competition ensures equal distribution of resources among individuals in a population', 'Competition leads to the development of new traits and adaptations in a population', 'Competition reduces the need for adaptations as individuals coexist peacefully', 'A'),
(4905, 137, 'Which of the following statements is true regarding sex-linked traits?', 'Sex-linked traits are located on the sex chromosomes', 'Sex-linked traits are inherited only from the mother', 'Sex-linked traits are more commonly observed in females', 'Sex-linked traits are not influenced by hormonal factors', 'A'),
(4906, 137, 'Which of the following is a plant hormone responsible for promoting cell elongation and growth?', 'Abscisic acid', 'Gibberellins', 'Ethylene', 'Cytokinins', 'B'),
(4907, 137, 'Which of the following is a primary source of pollution in aquatic ecosystems?', 'Soil erosion', 'Industrial discharge', 'Air pollution', 'Deforestation', 'B'),
(4908, 137, 'Which of the following mechanisms is responsible for providing support in plants?', 'Muscles and bones', 'Exoskeleton', 'Endocrine system', 'Cell walls and turgor pressure', 'D'),
(4909, 137, 'Metamorphosis is a biological process that involves', 'The growth and development of an organism from a zygote to an adult', 'The change in form and structure during the life cycle of certain organisms', 'The regeneration of lost body parts in an organism', 'The transformation of an organism from an adult stage to a larval stage', 'B'),
(4910, 137, 'Which of the following organs is primarily responsible for excretion in humans?', 'Liver', 'Pancreas', 'Kidneys', 'Lungs', 'C'),
(4911, 137, 'Which of the following is the correct classification of carbohydrates?', 'Lipid', 'Phytonutrient', 'Macronutrient', 'Micronutrient', 'C');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `subjectyear_id`, `question`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `correct_option`) VALUES
(4912, 137, 'Which of the following eye defects is caused by the inability of the eye to focus light on the retina?', 'Glaucoma', 'Myopia', 'Cataracts', 'Astigmatism', 'B'),
(4913, 137, 'Germination is the process in which a seed', 'Begins to photosynthesize', 'Develops into a mature plant', 'Absorbs nutrients from the soil', 'Breaks dormancy and starts to grow', 'D'),
(4914, 139, 'The major building block of an organism is...', 'Nitrogen', 'Carbon', 'Water', 'Sulphur', 'C'),
(4915, 139, 'The process by which plants lose water to the atmosphere is', 'Transpiration', 'Guttation', 'Translocation', 'Evaporation', 'A'),
(4916, 139, 'The formation of cilia and flagella in living cells is carried out with the help of', 'Ribosome', 'Lysosome', 'Centriole', 'Plastid', 'C'),
(4917, 139, 'The food nutrient with the highest energy value is', 'Protein', 'Carbohydrate', 'Lipid', 'Minerals', 'C'),
(4918, 139, 'Bilateral symmetry, cylindrical bodies and double openings are characteristic features of', 'Nematodes', 'Hydra', 'Protozoa', 'Protists', 'A'),
(4919, 139, 'Mouth part adapted for piercing and sucking is found in', 'Housefly', 'Grasshopper', 'Mosquito', 'Cockroach', 'C'),
(4920, 139, 'The web-feet of frogs and toads is basically for', 'Leaping', 'Walking', 'Swimming', 'Mating', 'C'),
(4921, 139, 'The part of the inner ear that is responsible for hearing is', 'Sacculus', 'Cochlea', 'Utriculus', 'Ampullae', 'B'),
(4922, 139, 'The changes of living organisms over generation is referred to as', 'Human evolution', 'Organic evolution', 'Physical evolution', 'Chemical evolution', 'B'),
(4923, 139, 'In a cross involving a heterozygous red flower plant (Rr) and a white flowered plant (rr). What is the probability that the offspring will be Rr?', '1/2', '1', '2', '1/4', 'A'),
(4924, 139, 'Inbreeding is highly discouraged in humans because it may', 'Increase the death rate of new born', 'Lead to the birth of dwarfs', 'Lead to high rate of competition among offspring', 'Lead to outbreak of hereditary diseases', 'D'),
(4925, 139, 'One main feature of trees in the savanna habitat is the possession of', 'Large, leathery leaves', 'Straight slender stems with branches near the top', 'Thin, smooth barks', 'Thick, corky bark', 'D'),
(4926, 139, 'Which of the following structures enables the exchange of gases in insects?', 'Skin', 'Tracheae', 'Malpighian tubules', 'Flame cell', 'B'),
(4927, 139, 'The total number of ATP produced during glycolysis is', '3 molecules', '2 molecules', '4 molecules', '6 molecules', 'B'),
(4928, 139, 'Bile is a greenish alkaline liquid which is stored in the', 'Gall bladder', 'Liver', 'Stomach', 'Pancreas', 'A'),
(4929, 139, 'A medium texture soil with high organic matter is', 'Clay', 'Loamy', 'Humus', 'Sandy', 'B'),
(4930, 139, 'One of the following is an example of discontinuous variation', 'Shape of the head', 'Height', 'Skin colour', 'Blood group', 'D'),
(4931, 139, 'The first organism evolved from which of the following habitat?', 'Terrestrial', 'Arboreal', 'Aquatic', 'Desert', 'C'),
(4932, 139, 'Which of these pair of substances must be present for a seed to germinate in a laboratory set-up?', 'Microbes and water', 'Heat and water', 'Soil and manure', 'Heat and microbe', 'B'),
(4933, 139, 'A fruit formed from one flower with many carpels is referred to as', 'Simple', 'Multiple', 'Aggregate', 'False', 'C'),
(4934, 139, 'Which of the following plant is found in the ground layer of a tropical rainforest in Nigeria?', 'Obecbe', 'Liverwort', 'Mahogany', 'Iroko', 'B'),
(4935, 139, 'Which of the following processes takes place in the carbon cycle?', 'Evaporation', 'Nitrification', 'Combustion', 'Transpiration', 'C'),
(4936, 139, 'Which of the following plants shows hypogeal germination?', 'Castor oil', 'Groundnut', 'Maize', 'Orange', 'C'),
(4937, 139, 'In vascular plants, xylem tissue is responsible for', 'Transportation of water', 'Translocation of food', 'Transportation of hormones', 'Storage of sugar', 'A'),
(4938, 139, 'The causative agent of tuberculosis is', 'Virus', 'Bacteria', 'Protozoa', 'Fungi', 'B'),
(4939, 139, 'Which of these is a respiratory organ in mammals?', 'Skin', 'Mouth', 'Heart', 'Lungs', 'D'),
(4940, 139, 'Which of Nigeria states is Northern guinea savanna located?', 'Borno', 'Kano', 'Oyo', 'Kwara', 'B'),
(4941, 139, 'Darwin\'s theory of evolution is based on the principle of', 'Use and disuse of organ', 'Natural selection', 'Acquired characteristics', 'Mutation', 'B'),
(4942, 139, 'Similar structures that are modified to work in different ways in different organisms are referred to as', 'Homologous structures', 'Analogous structures', 'Divergent structures', 'Convergent structures', 'A'),
(4943, 139, 'One of the ways of controlling Schistosomiasis is by', 'Destroying water snails and water weeds', 'Clearing the bushes around the house', 'Washing hands after using the toilet', 'Properly washing fruits before eating them', 'A'),
(4944, 139, 'The central nervous system comprises of', 'Brain and somatic', 'Brain and spinal cord', 'Spinal cord and somatic', 'Brain only', 'B'),
(4945, 139, 'Reproduction in paramecium is by', 'Binary fission', 'Budding', 'Spore formation', 'Fragmentation', 'A'),
(4946, 139, 'A community with a population of two million three hundred and ten thousand people living in an area of two thousand three hundred and ten square kilometres has a population density of', '10000', '10', '100', '1000', 'D'),
(4947, 139, 'A succession that occurs in an area where there are no pre-existing community is called', 'Tertiary succession', 'Primary succession', 'Post-primary succession', 'Secondary succession', 'B'),
(4948, 139, 'Which of the following processes releases oxygen to the atmosphere?', 'Respiration', 'Combustion', 'Decomposition', 'Photosynthesis', 'D'),
(4949, 139, 'The depressed side of paramecium which is lined with cilia leads to a tube-like structure called', 'Anal pore', 'Oral groove', 'Gullet', 'Food vacuole', 'B'),
(4950, 139, 'The rhizoid of liverwort is', 'Unicellular and unbranched', 'Multicellular and branched', 'Unicellular and branched', 'Multicellular and unbranched', 'A'),
(4951, 139, 'In glycolysis, glucose is broken down through series of reactions in the presence of enzyme and absence of oxygen to produce', 'Acetyl-coenzyme + ATP', 'Phosphorylated glucose', 'Pyruvic acid + ATP', 'Amino acid', 'C'),
(4952, 139, 'Gaseous exchange takes place through the plasma membrane in', 'Hydra', 'Paramecium', 'Flatworm', 'Earthworm', 'B'),
(4953, 139, 'One of the characteristics of secondary succession is that it', 'Starts on a bare surface', 'Takes longer time to reach climax', 'Starts on already colonized surface', 'Starts with low organism', 'C'),
(4954, 139, 'One of the components of xylem tissue is', 'Companion cell', 'Tracheid', 'Sieve tube', 'Epidermal', 'B'),
(4955, 139, 'Which of the following statements explains the theory of natural selection?', 'There is no struggle for existence', 'New species get better adaptation', 'The weaker offspring are eliminated', 'Unused structures disappear later', 'C'),
(4956, 139, 'The chemical and physical composition of soil is an example of', 'Climatic factor', 'Topographic factor', 'Edaphic factor', 'Chemical factor', 'C'),
(4957, 139, 'The abiotic factor that affect the population growth of an organism is', 'Predator', 'Rainfall', 'Food shortage', 'Disease', 'B'),
(4958, 139, 'The cells responsible for transmitting messages to the effectors are', 'Motor neurons', 'Sensory neurons', 'Hair cells', 'Relay neurons', 'A'),
(4959, 139, 'The oxygen transported to all parts of the body during blood circulation is used for the', 'Growth and development of cells', 'Removal of waste products', 'Release of energy from food', 'Formation of carboxyl haemoglobin', 'C'),
(4960, 139, 'After fertilization in plants, the zygote develops into', 'Fruit', 'An embryo', 'Seed', 'An endosperm', 'B'),
(4961, 139, 'Which of the following evidences of evolution employs the use of radio-isotope dating?', 'Comparative anatomy', 'Embryology', 'Fossil records', 'Vestigial organs', 'C'),
(4962, 139, 'The feeding relationship between ruminants and the bacteria in their digestive tract is', 'Saprophytic', 'Parasitic', 'Symbiotic', 'Heterotrophic', 'C'),
(4963, 139, 'A photosynthetic carnivorous plant which feeds on insects is', 'Parasitic', 'Saprophytic', 'Herbivorous', 'Insectivorous', 'D'),
(4964, 139, 'Xerophytes are mostly found in the', 'Arid land', 'Tropical rainforest', 'Montane forest', 'Sudan savanna', 'A'),
(4965, 139, 'In which zone of the marine habitat does the organisms require adaptation for attachment?', 'Supratidal', 'Subtidal', 'Intertidal', 'Benthic', 'C'),
(4966, 139, 'Energy transfer in plants and animals are in the form of', 'DNA', 'ATP', 'GTP', 'RNA', 'B'),
(4967, 140, 'Which of the following organisms contains Chlorophyll in its cells?', 'Caterpillar', 'Paramecium', 'Euglena', 'Grasshopper', 'C'),
(4968, 140, 'Species are groups of organisms that', 'Are of different origins and are always found together', 'Are of common origin but cannot interbreed freely', 'Have similar features and can interbreed freely', 'Resemble each other and occupy different niches', 'C'),
(4969, 140, 'A plant with short, vertical underground stem is a', 'Bulb', 'Corm', 'Rhizome', 'Tuber', 'B'),
(4970, 140, 'Which of the following organisms consists of unicellular cells joined to form a filament?', 'Amoeba', 'Spirogyra', 'Euglena', 'Chlamydomonas', 'B'),
(4971, 140, 'The structure in the cell that controls the movement of substances in and out of the cell is the', 'Cytoplasmic membrane', 'Nuclear membrane', 'Protoplasm', 'Endoplasmic reticulum', 'A'),
(4972, 140, 'The bursting of a red blood cell placed in a hypotonic solution is called', 'Crenation', 'Haemolysis', 'Plasmolysis', 'Cytolysis', 'B'),
(4973, 140, 'The function of the root hair in plants is to', 'Absorb soil water by the process of osmosis', 'Excrete water and mineral salts by simple diffusion', 'Purify the soil for the plant', 'Translocate manufactured food', 'A'),
(4974, 140, 'If a germinating seed is attached horizontally to a revolving kinostat, what would be the effect on the seedling after three days? The', 'Plumule will curve vertically upward while the radicle will not show any curvature', 'Radicle will curve towards the ground while the plumule will not show any curvature', 'Plumule and radicle will not show any curvature', 'Plumule will curve vertically upwards while the radicle will curve towards the ground', 'C'),
(4975, 140, 'The lumbar vertebra differs from the thoracic vertebra because it possesses a', 'Longer neural spine', 'Wider neural canal', 'Thicker centrum', 'Shorter transverse process', 'A'),
(4976, 140, 'Which of the following blood vessels carries oxygenated blood into the heart?', 'Pulmonary artery', 'Anterior vena cava', 'Pulmonary vein', 'Posterior vena cava', 'C'),
(4977, 140, 'Filtrates in the Bowman\'s capsule contain vitamins because', 'They have low molecular weight', 'Most of them are fat soluble', 'They cannot be reabsorbed into the blood', 'Little amount is required by the blood', 'A'),
(4978, 140, 'The structures that contain grey matter and white matter are found in the', 'Reproductive system', 'Nervous system', 'Respiratory system', 'Digestive system', 'B'),
(4979, 140, 'The condition necessary for reproduction to occur between plants P and Q after pollination is that plants P and Q should be', 'Of the same species', 'Brightly coloured', 'Well scented', 'Of different species', 'A'),
(4980, 140, 'The parachute-like tuft of hairs developed from the', 'Pedicel', 'Petals', 'Receptacle', 'Sepals', 'D'),
(4981, 140, 'Which of the following events does not occur in the light reaction stage of photosynthesis?', 'Chlorophyll absorbs sunlight', 'Carbon (IV) oxide combines with hydrogen', 'Photolysis of water occurs', 'Hydroxyl ions are produced', 'B'),
(4982, 140, 'The rate of photosynthesis decreases in a wilted herbaceous plant because the', 'Enzymes in the leaf were denatured', 'Chlorophyll in the leaves was not broken down', 'Amount of light reaching the plant was reduced', 'Amount of carbon dioxide entering the leaf decreases', 'D'),
(4983, 140, 'The element required for chlorophyll formation in plants is', 'Iron', 'Calcium', 'Phosphorus', 'Sulphur', 'A'),
(4984, 140, 'The process of food digestion in mammals would', 'Make energy immediately available to the body', 'Promote growth and repair of tissues', 'Provide sufficient food materials within the body', 'Render food substances soluble and absorbable', 'D'),
(4985, 140, 'Which of the following food substances would give a negative reaction with Benedict\'s reagent?', 'Fructose', 'Glucose', 'Galactose', 'Sucrose', 'D'),
(4986, 140, 'Sunlight is the major source of', 'Vitamin D', 'Vitamin C', 'Vitamin B', 'Vitamin A', 'A'),
(4987, 140, 'Discouraging the use of poison to kill fish in a large water body is a way of', 'Impoverishing the people', 'Conserving the fish species', 'Allowing the fittest organism to survive', 'Making the fish adapt to their environment', 'B'),
(4988, 140, 'The pathway through which nutrients are replenished and circulated in an ecosystem is called a', 'Cycle', 'Pyramid of energy', 'Pyramid of numbers', 'Food chain', 'A'),
(4989, 140, 'The illustration below is a food chain. Study it and answer questions 29 and 30. Grasses → Grasshoppers → Lizards → Hawks. Which of the following statements is not correct about the food chain? The number of', 'Grasses eaten by grasshoppers is greater than the number of grasshoppers', 'Grasses eaten by grasshoppers is fewer than the number of grasshoppers', 'Grasshoppers eaten by lizards is greater than the number of lizards', 'Lizards eaten by hawks is greater than the number of hawks', 'B'),
(4990, 140, 'Grasses → Grasshoppers → Lizards → Hawks. If the individual species of organisms in the food chain are counted and arranged as a pyramid, the result would be a pyramid of', 'Numbers', 'Energy', 'Biomass', 'Biomes', 'A'),
(4991, 140, 'Which of the following gases is released during the decomposition of organic matter?', 'Carbon(II) oxide', 'Sulphur (IV) oxide', 'Hydrogen Sulphide', 'Nitrous oxide', 'C'),
(4992, 140, 'An environmental problem caused by Sulphur (IV) oxide is', 'Acid rain', 'Deforestation', 'Global warming', 'Erosion', 'A'),
(4993, 140, 'The phenomenon by which a farmland that is left to fallow for several years develops into a forest is called', 'Succession', 'Afforestation', 'Population', 'Colonization', 'A'),
(4994, 140, 'An individual found a strange bird that is tagged as an endangered specie. What should the individual do?', 'Kill it', 'Take it to an aquatic environment', 'Return it to its natural habitat', 'Sell it at a very high price', 'C'),
(4995, 140, 'Which of the following traits is not inheritable? Ability to', 'Taste P.T.C', 'Roll the tongue', 'Move the ear', 'Roll the eyeball', 'C'),
(4996, 140, 'Which of the following statements is correct about the ABO blood group system?', 'Antigens are located on the surface of white blood cells', 'Antibodies are located in the blood plasma', 'Antibodies are located on the surface of the red blood cells', 'Antigens are located in the blood plasma', 'B'),
(4997, 140, 'A woman with blood group A gives birth to a child with blood group O. Which of the following blood groups cannot belong to the father?', 'B', 'A', 'AB', 'O', 'C'),
(4998, 140, 'The physical appearance of an organism is described as its', 'Phenotype', 'Genotype', 'Allele', 'Chromosome', 'A'),
(4999, 140, 'Mutation leads to evolution because it', 'Kills all organisms where it has occurred', 'Gives rise to offspring having same characteristics as the parents', 'Does not confer adaptability to the offspring', 'Gives rise to new individuals that differ from their parents', 'D'),
(5000, 140, 'The male and female gametes which bear genes for inheritance in plants are located in the', 'Anthers and petals', 'Sepals and petals', 'Stamens and pistils', 'Stamens and petals', 'C'),
(5001, 140, 'Which type of breeding is represented by industrial melanism in peppered moths?', 'Artificial selection', 'Natural selection', 'Inbreeding', 'Outbreeding', 'B'),
(5002, 140, 'In a test, a student paired some scientists with their famous work as shown below. Use it to answer questions 49 and 50. Scientist Famous work I. Charles Darwin → Preservation of some food with heat II. Gregor Mendel → Natural selection III. Jean Baptiste Lamarck → Inheritance of acquired characteristics IV. Louis Pasteur → Independent assortment of genes. The Scientists that are not correctly paired with their famous work are', 'I and II only', 'II and III only', 'I, II and IV', 'II, III and IV', 'C'),
(5003, 140, 'Which of the scientists were involved in the study of evolution? Scientist Famous work I. Charles Darwin → Preservation of some food with heat II. Gregor Mendel → Natural selection III. Jean Baptiste Lamarck → Inheritance of acquired characteristics IV. Louis Pasteur → Independent assortment of genes.', 'I and III', 'II and III', 'I, II and IV', 'II, III and IV', 'B'),
(5004, 134, 'Which of the following organelles is common to both plant and animal cells?', 'Cellulose cell wall', 'Chlorophyll', 'Cell membrane', 'Large vacuole', 'C'),
(5005, 134, 'A plant cell placed in a solution with a higher water potential will', 'Expand and then shrink', 'Enlarge and become turgid', 'Expand and then burst', 'Decrease in size and become flaccid', 'B'),
(5006, 134, 'Offspring formed by sexual reproduction exhibit more variation than those formed by asexual reproduction because', 'Greater amount of DNA is involved in sexual reproduction', 'Gametes of parents have different genetic composition', 'Genetic materials come from parents of two different species', 'Sexual reproduction is a lengthy process', 'B'),
(5007, 134, 'Radius and ulna are bones of the?', 'Pectoral girdle', 'Upper arm', 'Pelvic girdle', 'Lower arm', 'D'),
(5008, 134, 'The blood vessel which carries blood from the alimentary canal to the liver is the?', 'Hepatic artery', 'Hepatic vein', 'Hepatic portal vein', 'Mesenteric artery', 'C'),
(5009, 134, 'Detoxification of urea takes place in the?', 'Pancreas', 'Heart', 'Liver', 'Testes', 'C'),
(5010, 134, 'How many gametes are produced in the pollen grain of a flowering plant before fertilization?', 'One', 'Two', 'Three', 'Four', 'B'),
(5011, 134, 'Which of the following organisms does not undergo incomplete metamorphosis?', 'Locust', 'Grasshopper', 'Butterfly', 'Cockroach', 'C'),
(5012, 134, 'An enzyme reaction may begin to decline when?', 'The optimum temperature is attained', 'The pH of the medium is altered', 'There is an increase in substrate concentration', 'The atmospheric pressure is altered', 'B'),
(5013, 134, 'Which of the following factors is not necessary for photosynthesis?', 'Water', 'Carbon (IV) oxide', 'Wind', 'Sunlight', 'C'),
(5014, 134, 'Autotrophic nutrition is a process whereby an organism obtains food', 'By utilizing its stored energy', 'By synthesizing simple substances using energy', 'From other organisms in exchange for some products', 'In a synthesized form, from other living organisms', 'B'),
(5015, 134, 'The process that takes place at the light stage of photosynthesis is?', 'Splitting of water molecules to form hydrogen ions', 'Reduction of carbon (IV) oxide to form carbohydrate', 'Formation of two molecules of phosphoglyceric acid', 'Breaking down of ATP molecules to produce energy', 'A'),
(5016, 134, 'Which of the following plants is a carnivorous plant?', 'Gloriosa', 'Venus flytrap', 'Pitcher plant', 'Utricularia', 'B'),
(5017, 134, 'Plants and animals of an ecosystem make up a?', 'Habitat', 'Succession', 'Community', 'Population', 'C'),
(5018, 134, 'Rabbits cannot survive in an aquatic habitat because they have', 'No scales', 'No gills', 'Fore limbs', 'Lateral line', 'B'),
(5019, 134, 'The illustration below is a food chain. Grass → grasshopper → domestic fowl → hawk. What would happen if the population of domestic fowl decreases?', 'Grasshoppers would decrease', 'Hawks would increase', 'Grasshoppers would increase', 'Grasses available to grasshoppers would decrease', 'C'),
(5020, 134, 'Which of the following features is a characteristic of aquatic plants possession of?', 'Multiple epidermis', 'Heavily lignified tissue', 'Finely divided leaves', 'Succulent stem', 'C'),
(5021, 134, 'An association between living organisms in which one organism lives on and feeds at the expense of the other organism is known as?', 'Mutualism', 'Commensalism', 'Parasitism', 'Predation', 'C'),
(5022, 134, 'When a large number of organisms share limited resources, the result is?', 'Mutualism', 'Extinction', 'Commensalism', 'Competition', 'D'),
(5023, 134, 'Which of the following behaviours is correctly matched with the corresponding diseases?', 'Smoking cigarette / Liver cirrhosis, Lung cancer, AIDS', 'Having multiple sexual partners / Liver cirrhosis, syphilis, AIDS', 'Living near dirty gutter / Lung cancer, syphilis, river blindness', 'Eating uncooked meat / Dysentery, cholera, food poisoning', 'D'),
(5024, 134, 'Endangered species are organisms that are?', 'Likely to migrate to other favourable lands', 'Likely to disappear from the surface of the earth', 'Reproducing profusely in an area', 'Dangerous to humans and attacking other animals', 'B'),
(5025, 134, 'Which of the following practices is a wildlife conservation method?', 'Use of cover crops', 'Crop rotation', 'Mulching', 'Discouraging poaching', 'D'),
(5026, 134, 'Which of the following resources cannot be conserved?', 'Forest', 'Water', 'Soil', 'Garbage', 'D'),
