(6506, 3, 'What is the state of matter in which particles are widely spaced and move freely with high kinetic energy?', 'Liquid', 'Solid', 'Plasma', 'Gas', 'D'),
(6507, 3, 'Identify the reducing agent in the following reaction: Zn + CuSO4 → ZnSO4 + Cu', 'Cu', 'Zn', 'ZnSO4', 'CuSO4', 'B'),
(6508, 3, 'Balance the following redox reaction: Fe2O3 + CO → Fe + CO2', 'Fe2O3 + CO → 2Fe + 2CO2', '2Fe2O3 + 3CO → 4Fe + 3CO2', 'Fe2O3 + 2CO → 2Fe + 2CO2', 'Fe2O3 + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO2', 'D'),
(6509, 3, 'What is the trend for ionization energy across a period in the periodic table?', 'Increases from left to right.', 'Remains constant', 'Varies randomly', 'Decreases from left to right', 'A'),
(6510, 3, 'Which type of chemical combination involves the transfer of electrons from one atom to another, resulting in the formation of oppositely charged ions?', 'Ionic bonding', 'Hydrogen bonding', 'Covalent bonding', 'Metallic bonding', 'A'),
(6511, 3, 'Which of the following alkanes has a straight-chain structure?', 'Cyclopentane (C5H10)', 'Isobutane (C4H10)', '2-methyl propane (C4H10)', 'Pentane (C5H12)', 'D'),
(6512, 3, 'What is the product of the electrolysis of aqueous sodium chloride (NaCl) using inert electrodes?', 'Hydrogen gas at the cathode and chlorine gas at the anode', 'Hydrogen gas at the cathode and oxygen gas at the anode', 'Sodium metal at the cathode and chlorine gas at the anode', 'Sodium metal at the cathode and oxygen gas at the anode', 'A'),
(6513, 3, 'When an acidic solution is diluted, what happens to its pH?', 'It depends on the specific acid', 'It decreases', 'It remains the same', 'It increases', 'D'),
(6514, 3, 'Which of the following factors does NOT affect the rate of a chemical reaction?', 'Concentration of reactants', 'Presence of a catalyst', 'Molecular weight of products', 'Temperature', 'C'),
(6515, 3, 'What is the molar mass of water (H2O)?', '18 g/mol', '22 g/mol', '16 g/mol', '12 g/mol', 'A'),
(6516, 3, 'What is the chemical formula of rust, which is formed on the surface of iron in the presence of oxygen and moisture?', 'Fe3O4', 'FeO', 'Fe(OH)3', 'Fe2O3', 'D'),
(6517, 3, 'How many pi (π) bonds are there in an alkene with six carbon atoms?', '1', '6', '5', '3', 'A'),
(6518, 3, 'What is the principal ore of iron, from which iron is extracted?', 'Calcite', 'Bauxite', 'Magnetite', 'Hematite', 'D'),
(6519, 3, 'Which group does calcium belong to in the periodic table?', 'Alkaline earth metals', 'Halogens', 'Alkali metals', 'Transition metals', 'A'),
(6520, 3, 'Which of the following is a primary constituent of crude oil?', 'Pentane', 'Ethanol', 'Heptane', 'Methane', 'C'),
(6521, 3, 'What is the main source of carbon monoxide (CO) in urban areas?', 'Volcanic eruptions', 'Vehicle emissions', 'Forest fires', 'Industrial processes', 'B'),
(6522, 3, 'What is the empirical formula of a compound containing 40.00% carbon, 6.67% hydrogen, and 53.33% oxygen by mass?', 'C4H8O4', 'CH2O', 'C2H4O2', 'C3H6O3', 'B'),
(6523, 3, 'Which separation technique is used to separate different pigments in a mixture based on their affinity for a stationary phase and a mobile phase?', 'Chromatography', 'Filtration', 'Decantation', 'Distillation', 'A'),
(6524, 3, 'What is the common name for ethanoic acid?', 'Acetic acid', 'Butyric acid', 'Propionic acid', 'Formic acid', 'A'),
(6525, 3, 'What type of reaction is involved in the formation of alkanols from alkenes?', 'Elimination reaction', 'Redox reaction', 'Substitution reaction', 'Addition reaction', 'D'),
(6526, 3, 'What is the mass percentage of carbon (C) in methane (CH4)? (The molar mass of carbon is approximately 12 g/mol.)', '25%', '12%', '75%', '50%', 'C'),
(6527, 3, 'Which of the following is a common property of non-metals?', 'Exist as solids at room temperature', 'Tend to gain electrons in chemical reactions', 'High thermal conductivity', 'Readily form cations in chemical reactions', 'B'),
(6528, 16, 'Which of the following laws or theory cannot be explained by the application of the kinetic theory of gases?', 'Dalton\'s atomic theory', 'Charles\' law', 'Gay- lussac\'s law', 'Boyle\'s law', 'a'),
(6529, 16, 'The primary component of natural gas is', 'Butane', 'Ethane', 'Methane', 'Propane', 'c'),
(6530, 16, 'Thermal cracking of alkanes usually', 'Involves decomposition', 'Is an exothermic process', 'Produces only small alkanes', 'Requires hydrogen', 'a'),
(6531, 16, 'Carbon is deposited in the exhaust pipes of cars because of', 'Contamination of petrol with diesel', 'Presence of carbon petrol', 'Presence of additives in petrol', 'Incomplete combustion of petrol', 'd'),
(6532, 16, 'How many moles of copper would be deposited by passing 1 Faraday of electricity through a 2 CuCl 2 , solution?', '2', '1', '0.5', '0.25', 'c'),
(6533, 16, 'Alkenes can be manufactured by', 'Addition fo hydrogen to unsaturated vegetable oils', 'The cracking of hydrocarbons', 'Polymerization reactions', 'The combustion of alkanes', 'b'),
(6534, 16, 'Petrochemistry is an example of', 'Pure chemistry', 'Applied chemistry', 'Biochemistry', 'Environmental chemistry', 'b'),
(6535, 16, 'Species that occur in a reaction pathway but not in the overall reaction arc known as', 'Products', 'Inhibitors', 'Reactants', 'Intermediates', 'd'),
