(6537, 16, 'The best indicator to use for the titration of ethanoic acid with sodium hydroxide is', 'Methyl red', 'Methyl orange', 'Phenolphthalein', 'Screened methyl orange', 'c'),
(6538, 16, 'The reduction half equation half equation of the following reaction is: Zn (s) + CuSO 4 (aq) → ZnSO 4 (aq) + Cu (s)', 'CuSO 4 (s) + H 2 O → Cu (aq) 2+ + SO 4 2-', 'Cu (s) → Cu 2+ + 2e-', 'Cu 2+ + 2e- → Cu (s)', 'Zn (s) → Zn 2+ + 2e-', 'c'),
(6539, 16, '100cm 3 of a saturated solution of sodium tetraoxosulphate (VI) at 30 0 C contains 10.5g of the salt, what would be its solubility at this temperature? [Na 2 SO 4 =142]', '0.57 mol dm -3', '0.60 mol dm -3', '0.74 mol dm -3', '2.15 mol dm -3', 'c'),
(6540, 16, 'An example of a crystalline substance that does not possess water of crystallization is', 'Potassium trioxonitrate', 'Sodium trioxocarbonate (IV)', 'Iron (II) Tetraoxosulphate (VI)', 'Sodium tetraoxosulphate (VI)', 'a'),
(6541, 16, 'The salt solution formed from a reaction between ethanoic acid and sodium hydroxide solution would be', 'Basic', 'Acidic', 'Neutral', 'Amphoteric', 'a'),
(6542, 16, 'Which of the following reactions represent the hydrolysis of an alkanoate?', 'CH 3 COOH + C 2 H 5 OH ⇌ H+ CH 3 COOC 2 H 5 + H 2 O', 'CH 3 COOC 2 H 5 + H 2 O ⇌ H+ CH 3 COOH + C 2 H 5 OH', 'CH 3 COOCH 2 CH 3 CH 3 + H 2 O ⇌ H+ CH 3 COOH + CH 3 CH 2 OH', 'CH 3 COOH + OH- ⇌ H+ CH 3 COO- + H 2 O', 'b'),
