(6565, 16, 'Positive ions in a sea of electrons are found in', 'Covalent bonds', 'Dative bonds', 'Ionic bonds', 'Metallic bonds', 'd'),
(6566, 16, 'Dilute trioxonitrate (V) acid does not produce hydrogen when it reacts with metals because', 'It is a strong oxidizing agent', 'It reacts with the product', 'There is no visible reaction', 'It is a strong reducing agent', 'a'),
(6567, 16, 'How many moles are there in 3.0g of O 3? [O = 16]', '0.0093', '0.0930', '0.6250', '0.0625', 'd'),
