(6589, 17, 'The reaction represented by the equation: Ni2+(aq) + Fe(s) → Ni(s) + Fe2+(aq) is a redox reaction because', 'Ni2+ ions are oxidized and Fe acts as a oxidizing agent', 'Ni2+ ions are oxidized and Fe acts as a reducing agent', 'Ni2+ ions are reduced and Fe acts as an oxidizing agent', 'Ni2+ ions are reduced and Fe acts as a reducing agent.', 'D'),
