(6595, 17, 'The number of shared pair of electrons in a molecule of methane is', '2', '4', '6', '8', 'B'),
(6596, 17, 'Isotopes of the same element have similar chemical properties because they have the same number of', 'nuclides', 'protons', 'neutrons', 'atoms', 'B'),
(6597, 17, 'Which of the following household liquids would be effective in treating someone with too much acid in the stomach?', 'Strong salt solution with pH 7.0', 'Tomato juice with pH 4.1', 'Milk of Magnesia with pH 10.5', 'Black coffee with pH 5.0', 'C'),
(6598, 17, 'The percentage by mass of Oxygen in MgSO4.7H2O is [ Mr of MgSO4.7H2O = 246 ]', '26.0%', '45.5%', '71.5%', '84.0%', 'C'),
(6599, 17, 'Catalysts alter reaction rates by', 'providing an alternative reaction pathway', 'lowering the energy of reaction', 'increasing the surface area of reactants', 'aligning the reactant molecules properly', 'A'),
(6600, 17, 'Ethane of volume 400cm3 was completely burnt in excess oxygen according to the following equation: 2C2H6(g) + 7O2(g) → 6H2O(g) + 4CO2(g). Calculate the volume of steam that would be produced.', '200cm3', '400 cm3', '600 cm3', '1200 cm3', 'D'),
(6601, 17, 'A saturated solution at 300C will normally produce crystals at a temperature of', '500C', '400C', '350C', '200C', 'D'),
(6602, 17, 'The following organic compounds are polymers except', 'rubber', 'starch', 'proteins', 'fats', 'D'),
(6603, 17, 'According to the collision theory of reaction rates, which of the following conditions is not required for two molecules to react? The molecules must', 'come into contact without loss of energy on colliding with each other.', 'collide with enough energy to overcome the activation energy barrier', 'collide in an orientation that makes formation of product possible', 'possess enough speed to overcome intermolecular forces of attraction', 'A'),
