(6608, 17, 'Pure water contaminated with quicklime will have a pH of', '1', '6', '7', '8', 'D'),
(6609, 17, 'The electron configuration of 29 Cu is', '1S2 2S2 2P6 3S2 3P6 4S1 3d10', '1S2 2S2 2P6 3S2 3P64S3 3d9', '1S2 2S2 2P5 3S2 3P6 4S2 3d10', '1S2 2S2 2P6 3S2 3P2 4S1 3d10', 'A'),
(6610, 17, 'When s and p block elements react, the bond formed is', 'electrovalent', 'covalent', 'metallic', 'dative-covalent', 'A'),
(6611, 17, 'The hardest form of carbon is', 'charcoal', 'coke', 'diamond', 'graphite', 'C'),
(6612, 17, 'The metallic bonding in aluminium is strong because of large number of', 'delocalized electrons', 'immobile electrons', 'lone pair electrons', 'valence electrons', 'A'),
(6613, 17, 'When an element exists in two or more forms in the same physical state, it exhibits', 'isotope', 'allotropy', 'isobars', 'isomerism', 'B'),
(6614, 17, 'An atom of an element in the ground state contains 8 valence electrons. The element is considered as a', 'metal', 'semi-metal', 'noble gas', 'halogen', 'C'),
(6615, 17, 'The main function of limestone in the blast furnace during the extraction of iron is to', 'act as catalyst', 'remove impurities', 'act as a reducing agent', 'supply Carbon(IV) oxide', 'B'),
(6616, 17, 'Which of the following is a monomer of polythene?', 'Ethanol', 'Vinyl chloride', 'Ethene', 'Ethane', 'C'),
(6617, 17, 'Which of the following compounds is formed by the oxidation of ethanol?', 'C2H4CO2H', 'C2H5OH', 'CH3OH', 'CH3CO2H', 'D'),
(6618, 17, 'Tetraoxosulphate (VI) acid is considered as a heavy chemical because', 'its relative molecular mass is high', 'a high tonnage is produced every year', 'it is an inorganic chemical', 'it is used to manufacture heavy chemicals', 'B'),
