(6620, 17, 'The oxidation number of iron, in its free state is', '0', '+1', '+2', '+3', 'A'),
(6621, 17, 'Water pipes are produced from', 'polyethene', 'Perspex', 'polystyrene', 'poly vinyl chloride', 'D'),
(6622, 17, 'Consider the reaction represented by the following equation: xAl + yCl2 → zAlCl3', '2, 3 and 2', '2, 2 and 3', '1, 2 and 1', '1, 1 and 1', 'A'),
(6623, 145, 'A few grains of table salt were put in a cup of cold water, kept at constant temperature and left undistributed. Eventually all the water tested salty. This action is due to?', 'convection', 'osmosis', 'capillarity', 'diffusion', 'D'),
(6624, 145, 'The force required to make an object of mass m, travelling with velocity v, turn in a circle of radius r is', 'mv²/r', 'mr²v', 'mrv', 'mvr²', 'A'),
(6625, 145, 'A machine gun with a mass of 5kg fires a 50g bullet at a speed of 100 ms⁻¹. The recoil speed of the machine gun is', '0.5 ms⁻¹', '1.5 ms⁻¹', '1 ms⁻¹', '2 ms⁻¹', 'C'),
(6626, 145, 'If in a simple pendulum experiment the length of the inextensible string is increased by a factor of four, its period is increased by a factor of?', '4', 'π/2', '1/4', '2', 'D'),
(6627, 145, 'In what range of temperature is the expansion of water anomalous?', '+208°C to +212°C', '-80°C to -76°C', '0°C to +4°C', '-4°C to +0°C', 'C'),
(6628, 145, 'Which of the following statements about radioactivity is true? (i) Alpha particle is positively charged (ii) Beta particle is negatively charged (iii) Gamma ray is neutral (iv) Beta particle has the same mass as helium atom (v) Gamma ray is charged.', 'i, ii, iii, iv only', 'i, ii, iii only', 'iv and v only', 'i, ii and v only', 'B'),
(6629, 145, 'In the study of Physics, temperature and heat are often confused with each other. Which of the following statements correctly defines these two elements?', 'Temperature is a measure of the average kinetic energy of the molecules of a substance', 'Heat is a measure of the total kinetic energy of the molecules in a system', 'Different materials require different amounts of heat to cause a given change in temperature', 'All of the above', 'D'),
