(6747, 19, 'The distance between a node and its adjacent antinode of a transverse wave is equal to?', 'half of the wavelength', 'the wavelength', 'thrice the wavelength', 'quarter of the wavelength', 'D'),
(6748, 19, 'Which of the sketched graphs above illustrates the correct variation of the gravitational force, Fg between two objects and the distance, d, between the centre', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'A'),
(6749, 19, 'Which of the following actions will increase capacitance of a parallel plate capacitor? I. Decreasing the distance between the plates. II. Increasing the distance between the plates. III. Increasing the area of the plates overlap. IV. Avoiding the use of dielectric between the plates', 'I and III only', 'II and III only', 'I and IV', 'III and IV only', 'A'),
(6750, 19, 'A metallic sphere is heated from 27°C to 200°C without change of state. Which of the following changes would have resulted from the heating?', 'No changes occur in its volume and density', 'Its volume increases and its density increases', 'Its volume increases and its density decreases', 'Its volume increases without a change in density', 'C'),
(6751, 19, 'The acceleration of a moving object can be determined from the?', 'slope of its distance-time graph', 'area under its distance-time graph', 'slope of its velocity-time graph', 'area under its velocity-time graph', 'C'),
(6752, 19, 'A student wishes to measure the potential difference across a resistor, R. She has a galvanometer, G and some connecting wires. What else does she need?', 'high value resistor connected in parallel with G', 'low value resistor connected in parallel with G', 'low value resistor connected in series with G', 'high value resistor connected in series with G', 'D'),
(6753, 19, 'The handle of a screw jack is 35cm long and the pitch of the screw is 0.5cm. What force must be applied at the end of the handle to lift a load of 2000N, if the efficiency of the jack is 30% [π = 22/7]?', '152.0N', '132.0N', '15.2N', '440.0N', 'C'),
(6754, 19, 'The inductive reactance in a circuit of frequency 100Hz is 1 ohm. Calculate the inductance of the inductor [π = 3.14]', '2.00 × 10⁻³ H', '1.59 × 10⁻³ H', '1.09 × 10⁻³ H', '6.28 × 10⁻³ H', 'B'),
(6755, 19, 'The diagram above illustrates the velocity-time graph of a body. Calculate the distance covered by the body during the motion', '15m', '84m', '72m', '48m', 'B'),
(6756, 19, 'An atom that emits an α-particle?', 'may become a different element', 'becomes a different isotope of the element', 'daughter with increased mass', 'becomes a daughter of a different element always', 'A'),
(6757, 19, 'Which of the following units is equivalent to the unit of electric current?', 'C s⁻¹', 'W', 'J s⁻¹', 'C', 'A'),
(6758, 19, 'A ball is swung in a horizontal circle of centre O with a constant speed. What is the direction of its acceleration?', 'Away from O', 'Along the circumference of the circle', 'Toward centre O', 'Along a tangent to the circle', 'C'),
(6759, 19, 'Which of the following statements is an effect of compressing gas molecules at constant temperature?', 'The pressure on the molecules decreases', 'The molecules gain more kinetic energy', 'The molecules make more impact per second on the walls of the container', 'The molecules increase in size', 'C'),
(6760, 19, 'The diagram above is an illustration of an a.c. circuit. Calculate the reactance of the capacitor.', '2016Ω', '2000Ω', '200Ω', '4000Ω', 'C'),
(6761, 19, 'A current of 2A passes through a wire of resistance 4Ω for 3 minutes. Calculate the energy lost.', '960J', '1440J', '2880J', '48J', 'C'),
(6762, 19, 'Which of the following statements about the universal gravitational constant, G, is true?', 'It is fundamental quantity', 'It has dimension M⁻¹L³T⁻²', 'Its S.I. unit is N m² kg', 'It is a vector quantity', 'B'),
(6763, 19, 'The sketched graph above represents a progressive wave moving from the left to the right. The period of the wave is 0.125s. Determine the values of the amplitude and wavelength, respectively, of the wave.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A'),
(6764, 19, 'Determine the speed of the wave.', '64 cm/s', '32 cm/s', '24 cm/s', '72 cm/s', 'B'),
(6765, 19, 'Which of the following curved surfaces will produce a real image? I. Concave mirror II. Convex mirror III. Diverging lens IV. Converging lens', 'I and III only', 'I, II and IV only', 'II, III and V only', 'I and IV only', 'D'),
(6766, 19, 'The components of vectors Q and R are (-3.0, 5.5) and (9.2, 4.4) respectively. Determine the components of Q + R.', '(3.7, 7.4)', '(6.2, 9.9)', '(2.5, -4.8)', '(14.7, 1.4)', 'B'),
(6767, 19, 'Which of the arrangements of radiations below shows decreasing order of wavelengths?', 'X-rays > radio waves > infrared radiations', 'Radio waves > infrared radiations > X-rays', 'Infrared radiations > radio waves > X-rays', 'X-rays > infrared radiations > radio waves', 'B'),
(6768, 19, 'An electric pressing iron is connected to the mains using an insulated wire. The wire becomes very hot. The heat generated in the wire can be minimized by replacing the wire with one of?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A'),
(6769, 19, 'In the diagram above, a bulb is lit by drawing 2.0A from 440V a.c. source. Calculate the cost of keeping the bulb on for two days at $0.40 per kilowatt-hour.', '$16.90', '$84.48', '$1690.00', '$8.48', 'A'),
(6770, 19, 'A wire of cross-sectional area 2π × 10⁻⁸ m² and resistivity 1.1 × 10⁻⁸ Ωm, has a resistance of 21Ω. Calculate the length of the wire. [π = 22/7]', '180m', '140m', '120m', '0.240m', 'C'),
(6771, 19, 'Which of the following statements best describes the particles in a solid at room temperature? They are', 'far apart and moving randomly', 'close together and vibrating', 'close together and stationary', 'close together and moving randomly', 'B'),
(6772, 19, 'A man weighing 200N runs up a staircase in 5s. If the height of the staircase is 9m, calculate the power of the man.', '1000W', '360W', '40W', '1800W', 'B'),
(6773, 19, 'A rotating disc contains a set of holes in a circle. An air jet is directed onto the holes and a note of frequency 480Hz is produced. If the number of holes is 20, calculate the speed of rotation of the disc.', '10 rev/s', '20 rev/s', '24 rev/s', '8 rev/s', 'C'),
(6774, 19, 'A force of 10N, acting continuously, increases the kinetic energy of an object from 20J to 60J. Find the distance moved by the object.', '200m', '40m', '4m', '400m', 'C'),
(6775, 19, 'An electric circuit consists of a resistor, a battery and a key. If the voltage of the battery is increased, there would be an increase in the?', 'current and resistance only', 'current, resistance and temperature', 'current and temperature only', 'resistance and temperature only', 'C'),
(6776, 19, 'A radioactive material has a half-life of 1.0 hour. If 200.0g of it was present at 6 a.m. on a certain day, how many grams will have decayed by 9 a.m. on the same day?', '175.0g', '150.0g', '100.0g', '187.5g', 'A'),
(6777, 19, 'The following statements about a loudspeaker are correct except?', 'it contains a permanent magnet', 'sound signal converted to varying current signal enters the speech coil', 'the current in the speech coil creates a magnetic force on the coil', 'the magnetic force on the speech coil is uni-directional', 'D'),
(6778, 19, 'An ice cube has mass of 20g at -5°C. Calculate the energy required to raise its temperature to 0°C. [Specific heat capacity of ice = 2.1 J/g°C]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A'),
(6779, 19, 'A stone is thrown horizontally with initial velocity 15 m/s from a tower 20m high. How long does it take to reach the ground? [g = 10 m/s²]', '2s', '4s', '5s', '1s', 'A'),
(6780, 19, 'Which of the following statements is not a characteristic of a plane progressive wave?', 'Energy travels out through the medium', 'Neighboring points along the profile possess different amplitudes', 'Neighboring points along the profile possess the same amplitude', 'Neighboring particles vibrate with different phase', 'B'),
(6781, 19, 'The electrons in a cathode-ray tube are produced by?', 'heating a metal filament', 'ionization of the air', 'applying a magnetic field to the y-plates', 'applying an electric field to the x-plates', 'A'),
(6782, 19, 'Which of the following statements about distance and displacement is not correct?', 'Displacement is a vector quantity', 'Distance has dimension', 'Displacement is measured in meters', 'Distance is a vector quantity', 'D');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `subjectyear_id`, `question`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `correct_option`) VALUES
(6783, 19, 'A note produced by an instrument is distinguished from a similar note produced by another instrument by the?', 'intensity', 'pitch', 'overtones', 'loudness', 'C'),
(6784, 19, 'According to Pascals principle, the pressure in a fluid is always?', 'dependent on density of the fluid', 'distributed partially in all directions', 'transmitted equally in all directions', 'increasing with height', 'C'),
(6785, 19, 'Which of the following set of quantities have members which are all vectors?', 'Pressure, energy and force', 'Force, displacement and momentum', 'Distance, acceleration and work', 'Density, volume and weight', 'B'),
(6786, 19, 'If the relative humidity of the atmosphere increases, the rate of evaporation of sweat from the human body?', 'decreases', 'remains the same', 'increases then decreases', 'increases', 'A'),
(6787, 19, 'Which of the following factors is not among that determines the resistance of a wire?', 'mass', 'cross-sectional area', 'length', 'material', 'A'),
(6788, 19, 'Which of the following scientist suggested that moving particles exhibit wave properties?', 'Isaac Newton', 'Ernest Rutherford', 'Louis de Broglie', 'J.J. Thompson', 'C'),
(6789, 6, 'Which of these is a derived unit?', 'Kilogram', 'Metre', 'Newton', 'Second', 'C'),
(6790, 6, 'A bar magnet is divided into two pieces, which of the following statement is correct?', 'two new magnets are created', 'the magnetic field of each separate piece becomes stronger', 'the electric field is created', 'the bar magnet is demagnetized', 'A'),
(6791, 6, 'Consider the wave equation y = 5mm sin [1cm-1 x - 60s-1 t]. The wave number is?', '0.1 cm-1', '10 cm-1', '1.0 cm-1', '2 cm-1', 'A'),
(6792, 6, 'An object 40 cm high is 30 cm from the pin hole camera. If the height of the image formed is 20 cm. What is the distance of the image from the pin height?', '15 cm', '70 cm', '40 cm', '40 cm', 'A'),
(6793, 6, 'A bar magnet is placed near and lying along the axis of a solenoid connected to a galvanometer. The pointer of the galvanometer shows no deflection when?', 'the magnet is moved towards the stationary solenoid', 'there is no relative motion', 'the magnet is moved away from the stationary solenoid', 'the solenoid is moved away from the stationary magnet', 'B'),
(6794, 6, 'Tyres are treaded to?', 'increase weight of tyres', 'increase friction', 'increase its longevity', 'look good', 'B'),
(6795, 6, 'A car starts from rest and covers a distance of 40 m in 10 s. Calculate the magnitude of its acceleration', '3.20 ms-2', '0.25 ms-2', '0.80 ms-2', '4.00 ms-2', 'C'),
(6796, 6, 'The relationship between the coefficient of linear expansion (α) and volumetric expansion (γ) is', 'γ = α', 'γ = 2α', 'γ = 3α', 'γ = 1/3α', 'C'),
(6797, 6, 'Which of the following is not a consequence of hydrogen bubbles covering the copper plate of a primary cell?', 'formation of hydrogen bubbles on the electrode', 'increase in the resistance of the cell', 'local action', 'polarization', 'C'),
(6798, 6, 'A cell whose internal resistance is 0.55 Ω delivers a current of 4 A to an external resistor. The lost voltage of the cell is?', '4.00 V', '2.20 V', '0.15 V', '8.00 V', 'B'),
(6799, 6, 'Which of the following liquid is a poor conductor of electricity?', 'Distilled water', 'Tap water', 'Sea water', 'Drinking water', 'A'),
(6800, 6, 'An isotope has an initial activity of 120 Bq. 6 days later its activity is 15 Bq. The half-life is?', '3 days', '2 days', '1 day', '4 days', 'B'),
(6801, 6, 'The secondary pigments consist of?', 'blue, green, and violet', 'yellow, green, and magenta', 'magenta, yellow, and cyan', 'red, green, and blue', 'C'),
(6802, 6, 'A person standing waist-deep in a swimming pool appears to have short legs because of light?', 'diffraction', 'refraction', 'reflection', 'interference', 'B'),
(6803, 6, 'A tuning fork having a frequency of 312 Hz emits a wave which has a wavelength of 1.10 m. Calculate the velocity of sound', '312.0 ms-1', '110.0 ms-1', '343.2 ms-1', '686.4 ms-1', 'C'),
(6804, 6, 'When the plate area of a capacitor increases?', 'the voltage can withstand increase', 'the capacitance decreases', 'the capacitance is unaffected', 'the capacitance increases', 'D'),
(6805, 6, 'A magnet relay is a device used for?', 'reading the magnitude of magnetic flux', 'controlling another circuit carrying larger current', 'turning in sports', 'storing magnetic field', 'B'),
(6806, 6, 'According to kinetic molecular model in gases,', 'the particles are closely packed together; they occupy minimum space are usually arranged in a regular pattern', 'the particles vibrate about fixed positions and are held together by the strong intermolecular bonds between them', 'the molecules are very far apart and occupy all the spaces made available to them', 'the particles occur in clusters with molecules slightly further apart', 'C'),
(6807, 6, 'A current of 0.5 A flows through a resistor when connected to a 40 V battery. How much energy is dispatched in 2 minutes?', '2400 J', '9600 J', '1500 J', '1200 J', 'A'),
(6808, 6, 'For a pear-shaped conductor shown above, the concentration of charge on the outside is highest at?', 'X', 'Z', 'Y', 'K', 'B'),
(6809, 6, 'Which of these is a second-class lever?', 'sugar tongs', 'claw hammer', 'plier', 'wheelbarrow', 'D'),
(6810, 6, 'In the formation of sea breeze, wind blows from?', 'sky to land', 'sea to sky', 'land to sea', 'sea to land', 'D'),
(6811, 6, 'Which component of fiber-optic connector has a provision of entry for the fibre along with the fixation to connector housing?', 'coupling device', 'cable', 'ferrule', 'connector housing', 'C'),
(6812, 6, 'In order to view the sun, the most suitable instrument to use is?', 'helioscope', 'telescope', 'stroboscope', 'sun meter', 'A'),
(6813, 6, 'The eclipse of the moon occurs when?', 'the moon reflects the rays from the sun to the earth', 'the moon comes exactly between the earth and the sun', 'the earth comes exactly between the moon and the sun', 'the sun comes exactly between the earth and the moon', 'C'),
(6814, 6, 'The gravitational pull on the moon is 1/6 that of the earth. If a body weighs 6.0 N on the moon, what will be the weight on the earth?', '6.0 N', '5.0 N', '12.0 N', '36.0 N', 'D'),
(6815, 6, 'The amount of energy required to change a kilogram of ice block into water without a change in temperature is?', 'specific latent heat of fusion of ice', 'specific heat capacity of ice', 'heat capacity of ice', 'specific heat of vaporization of ice', 'A'),
(6816, 6, 'Which expression gives magnetic flux?', 'qVB sinθ', 'μ0I/2πr', 'BA cos θ', '-N dΦ/dt', 'C'),
(6817, 6, 'The graph of pressure (P) against the reciprocal of the volume (1/V) in Boyle\'s law is a?', 'hyperbola', 'parabola', 'curve', 'straight line', 'D'),
(6818, 6, 'What quantity of heat is required to convert 20 g of ice at 0°C to water at the same temperature? (Specific latent heat of ice = 336 J/g)', '6.72 × 10³ J', '5.38 × 10³ J', '6.72 × 10³ J', '1.35 × 10³ J', 'C'),
(6819, 6, 'A train of mass 1600 kg attains a speed of 25 ms-1 in 20 seconds. The power developed in the engine is?', '2.5 kW', '80 kW', '25 kW', '50 kW', 'D'),
(6820, 6, 'The main factor which affects the speed of sound wave is the?', 'properties of the medium', 'amplitude of the sound wave', 'intensity of the sound wave', 'loudness of the sound wave', 'A'),
(6821, 6, 'A semiconductor is formed by?', 'co-ordinate bonds', 'electrovalent bonds', 'a substance free of bonds', 'covalent bonds', 'D'),
(6822, 6, 'One of the following is a scalar quantity?', 'weight', 'momentum', 'potential energy', 'displacement', 'C'),
(6823, 6, 'The mercury column in the barometer at notational atmospheric pressure has a height of?', '0.76 cm at sea level', '760 cm at sea level', '7.6 cm at sea level', '76 cm at sea level', 'D'),
(6824, 6, 'If an object just begins to slide on a surface inclined at 30° to the horizontal, the coefficient of friction is?', '√3', '√3/2', '1/√2', '1/√3', 'D'),
(6825, 20, 'The area under a force-time graph represents', 'change in kinetic energy', 'change in momentum', 'change in work done', 'change in internal energy', 'B'),
(6826, 20, 'From the principle of flotation, a body sinks in a fluid until it displace a quantity equal to its own?', 'density', 'mass', 'weight', 'volume', 'C'),
(6827, 20, 'The length of a simple pendulum is increased by a factor of four. By what factor is its period increase?', '0.5π', '2', '2π', '4', 'B'),
(6828, 20, 'The linear expansivity, α, and cubic expansivity, γ, of a material are related by the equation?', 'γ = α', 'γ = 3α', 'γ = 2α', 'γ = 1/3α', 'B'),
(6829, 20, 'Suppose three identical steel balls Q, R, and S, are placed on an undulating ground as illustrated in the diagram above. Which of the balls is/are in neutral equilibrium?', 'S only', 'Q only', 'R only', 'Q and S only', 'A'),
(6830, 20, 'Which of the illustrated graphs above represents a body moving with uniform retardation?', 'A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'C'),
(6831, 20, 'The correct relationship between the displacement, s, of a particle initially at rest in a linear motion and the time, t, is?', 's ∝ t-2', 's ∝ t-1', 's ∝ t', 's ∝ t2', 'D'),
(6832, 20, 'The joule is equivalent to?', 'Kg m2 s-1', 'Kg2 m s-2', 'Kg m2 s-2', 'Kg m s-1', 'C'),
(6833, 20, 'Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct about a fixed mass of gas compressed in an inexpansible container; I. The average speed of the molecules increases II. The temperature of the gas increases III. The molecules hit the walls of the container more often than before the compression', 'I only', 'I and II only', 'I, II, and III only', 'I and III', 'C'),
(6834, 20, 'An example of a mechanical wave is', 'water waves', 'radio waves', 'x-rays', 'light rays', 'A'),
(6835, 20, 'Which of the following descriptions of the image formed by a plane mirror is not correct. the image is---', 'erect and of the same size as the object', 'laterally inverted and of the same size as the object', 'erect and bigger than the object', 'virtual and of the same size', 'C'),
(6836, 20, 'The efficiency of a wheel and axle is 100% and the ratio of their radii is 5:1. calculate the effort required to lift a load of mass 20kg using this machine, [g = 10m s-2]', '20N', '25N', '40N', '100N', 'C'),
(6837, 20, 'A freely suspended compass needle on the earth\'s surface settles in a plane called', 'geographic meridian', 'magnetic meridian', 'magnetic declination', 'isogamals', 'B'),
(6838, 20, 'An object is placed at different distances, u, from a converging lens of focal length, 15.0cm. For what value of u does the lens act as a microscope?', 'u = 15cm only', 'u = 30cm only', 'u < 15cm only', 'u > 30cm only', 'C'),
(6839, 20, 'The periodic rise and fall in the intensity of sound produced when two notes of nearly equal frequencies are sounded together is called?', 'doppler effect', 'beat', 'interference', 'resonance', 'B'),
(6840, 20, 'The power of the lens is +2.5D. What is the radius of the curvature?', '2.5 cm', '25.0 cm', '40.0 cm', '80.0 cm', 'C'),
(6841, 20, 'The soft-iron core placed inside a galvanometer is to', 'make the deflection of the needle proportional to the current', 'increase the sensitivity of the galvanometer', 'decrease the magnetic flux produced by the magnet', 'make the permanent magnet stronger', 'B'),
(6842, 20, 'Current is passed through two parallel conductors in the same direction. If the conductors are placed near each other, they will', 'move in a circle', 'repel each other', 'remain stationary', 'attract each other', 'D'),
(6843, 20, 'The period of a 10kHz radio wave traveling at 108 ms-1 is', '3.0 × 10-5s', '1.0 × 10-4s', '1.0 × 104s', '1.0 × 10-4s', 'B'),
(6844, 20, 'The magnetic material produced from the chemical combination of metal oxides and has a very high resistance to electric current is called', 'ferrite substance', 'paramagnetic substance', 'ferromagnetic substance', 'diamagnetic substance', 'A'),
(6845, 20, 'A body of mass, M, moving with velocity, V, has a wavelength, λ, associated with it. This phenomenon is called', 'photoelectric effect', 'heisenberg\'s uncertainty principle', 'compton effect', 'wave-particles paradox', 'D'),
(6846, 20, 'Which of the following statements about a straight current-carrying wire placed in a uniform magnetic field is correct? The wire experiences', 'maximum motor force if the current reverses its direction', 'no motor force if it is parallel to the field', 'no motor force if it is perpendicular to the field', 'a motor force with constant direction if either the current or the magnetic field is reversed', 'B'),
(6847, 20, 'Three cells each of emf, 1.0 V, and internal resistance, 2 Ω, are connected in parallel across a 3Ω resistor. Determine the current in the resistor.', '0.90A', '0.39A', '0.30A', '0.01A', 'C'),
(6848, 20, 'Which of the following statements about electric potential energy is not correct?', 'The electric potential energy of a positively charged particle increases when it moves to a point of higher potential', 'The electric potential energy of a negatively charged particle increases when it moves to a point of lower potential', 'The electric potential energy of a positively charged particle decreases when it moves to a point of higher potential', 'The work done in taking a charged particle around a closed path in an electric field is zero.', 'C'),
(6849, 20, 'A galvanometer with a full-scale deflection of 20mA is converted to read 8V by connecting a 395Ω resistor in series with it. Determine the internal resistance of the galvanometer', '2.5Ω', '5.0Ω', '8.0Ω', '10.0Ω', 'B'),
(6850, 20, 'An inductor of inductance 10 H is connected across an a.c circuit source of 50 V, 100 Hz. What is the current in the circuit? [π = 3.14]', '0.200A', '0.070A', '0.050A', '0.008A', 'D'),
(6851, 20, 'The speed of fast-moving neutrons in a nuclear reactor can be reduced by using?', 'graphite rods', 'concrete shield', 'iron rods', 'boron rods', 'A'),
(6852, 20, 'In a series R-L-C circuit at resonance, impedance is', 'maximum', 'minimum', 'capacitive', 'inductive', 'B'),
(6853, 20, 'A lamp is rated 240 V, 60 W. Determine the resistance of the lamp when lit?', '120Ω', '240Ω', '540Ω', '960Ω', 'D'),
(6854, 20, 'One major reason why electrical appliances in homes are normally earthed is that the', 'person touching the appliance is safe from electric shock', 'appliances are maintained at a higher p.d. than the earth', 'appliances are maintained at a lower p.d. than the earth', 'appliances are maintained at the same p.d. with that of the earth', 'A'),
(6855, 20, 'In doping an intrinsic semiconductor to produce a p-type semiconductor,', 'the semiconductor is heated up', 'a donor element is added', 'an acceptor element is added', 'the semiconductor is conducted to a battery', 'C'),
(6856, 20, 'Arrange the following radiations in order of increasing ionization of air. I. Alpha II. Gamma III. Beta', 'I < II < III', 'II < III < I', 'III < I < II', 'I < III < II', 'B'),
(6857, 20, 'If the kinetic energy of an electron is 100eV, what is the wavelength of the de-Broglie wave associated with it? [h = 6.6 × 10-34 J s, e = 1.6 × 10-19 C, me = 9.1 × 10-31 kg]', '1.22 × 10-10 m', '4.10 × 10-10 m', '3.90 × 10-10 m', '5.50 × 10-14 m', 'A'),
(6858, 20, 'Gamma rays are produced when?', 'high velocity electrons are abruptly stopped in metals', 'energy changes occur within the nuclei of atoms', 'energy changes occur within the electronic structure of atoms', 'electrons are deflected in very strong magnetic fields', 'B'),
(6859, 20, 'The half-life of a radioactive substance is 15 hours. If at some instance, the sample has a mass of 512 g, calculate the time it will take 7/8 of the sample to decay', '15 hours', '30 hours', '45 hours', '60 hours', 'C'),
(6860, 20, 'When the direction of vibration of the particles of a medium is perpendicular to the direction of propagation of a wave, the wave is said to be', 'longitudinal', 'transverse', 'mechanical', 'a sound wave', 'B'),
(6861, 20, 'A hunter fires a gun at a point 408 m away from a cliff. If he hears an echo 2.4 s later, determine the speed of the sound wave', '340 ms-1', '380 ms-1', '400 ms-1', '680 ms-1', 'A'),
(6862, 20, 'The distance between the fixed points of a mercury-in-glass thermometer is 30 cm. Determine the temperature when the mercury level is 10.5 cm above the lower fixed point', '28.6°C', '30.0°C', '35.0°C', '40.5°C', 'C'),
(6863, 20, 'Which of the following statements about electromagnetic waves is not correct?', 'They carry energy as they travel through space.', 'They travel with the speed of light.', 'They are longitudinal.', 'The electric and magnetic fields are at right angles to each other', 'C'),
(6864, 20, 'The diameter of a brass ring at 30°C is 50.0cm. To what temperature must this ring be heated to increase its diameter to 50.29cm? [linear expansivity of brass = 1.9 × 10-5 K-1]', '152.6°C', '182.6°C', '306.1°C', '335.3°C', 'D'),
(6865, 20, 'Which of the following concepts is a method of heat transfer that does not require a material medium?', 'Conduction', 'Diffusion', 'Convection', 'Radiation', 'D'),
(6866, 20, 'Which of the following statements about light travelling from one material medium to another is not correct?', 'The refracted angle is less than the incident angle if the speed is higher in the first material', 'Its wavelength does not change', 'It bends away from the normal if the speed is lower in the first material', 'Its frequency changes.', 'B'),
(6867, 20, 'The engine of a car provides a forward force of 1240N and the total resistive force on the car is 800N. If the mass of the car is 1220kg, determine the distance the car has to travel from rest before acquiring a speed of 4ms-1.', '44.0 m', '22.2 m', '11.1 m', '5.5 m', 'B'),
(6868, 20, 'A quantity of water at 0°C is heated to 30°C. For each degree rise in temperature, its density will', 'rise steadily', 'fall steadily', 'fall and then rise', 'rise and then fall', 'C'),
(6869, 20, 'A small object of mass 50g is released from a point A. Determine the velocity of the object when it reaches a point B, a vertical distance of 30m below A. [g = 10ms-2]', '1.5 ms-1', '6.0 ms-1', '17.3 ms-1', '24.5 ms-1', 'D'),
(6870, 20, 'Molecules move in random motion within a liquid. The total internal energy of the liquid depends on all of the following except its?', 'temperature', 'mass', 'specific heat capacity', 'melting point', 'D'),
(6871, 20, 'The viscosity of a fluid depends on the following factors except the?', 'relative motion between the layers of the fluid', 'nature of the material of the fluid', 'surface area of the fluid in contact', 'normal reaction in the fluid', 'D'),
(6872, 20, 'Using vernier calipers, which of the following readings gives the correct measurement for the length of a rod?', '4.1 cm', '4.13 cm', '125 cm', '1254 cm', 'B'),
(6873, 20, 'The basic principle of operation of a beam balance is', 'Hooke\'s law', 'Archimedes principle', 'law of flotation', 'principle of moments', 'D'),
