(6990, 8, 'A rectifier is a device that changes', 'D.C to D.C', 'D.C to A.C', 'A.C to A.C', 'A.C to D.C', 'D'),
(6991, 8, 'The dimension of young\'s modulus, E is given by', 'MLT^-1', 'MT^-2', 'ML^-1T^-2', 'M^-1T', 'C'),
(6992, 8, 'The moon\'s acceleration due to gravity is 1/6 of the earth\'s value. The weight of a bowling ball on the moon would be', '6 times its weight on the earth', '1/6 of its weight on the earth', '36 times its weight on the earth', 'equal to its weight on the earth', 'B'),
(6993, 8, 'If a sheet of an insulating material is inserted between the plates of an air capacitor, the capacitance will', 'become zero', 'decrease', 'increase', 'remain unchanged', 'C'),
(6994, 8, 'Convert 60°C to degree Fahrenheit', '111.15', '115.56', '132.23', '140.00', 'D'),
(6995, 8, 'A sonometer\'s fundamental note is 50Hz, what is the new frequency when the tension is four times the original?', '25Hz', '100Hz', '200Hz', '250Hz', 'B'),
(6996, 8, 'Which of the following is not a part of model rocket?', 'The body tube', 'The nose cones', 'The fin', 'Not recovery devices', 'D'),
(6997, 8, 'A thick glass tumbler cracks when boiling water is poured into it because', 'The inside expands more rapidly than the outside', 'The inside expands less rapidly than the outside', 'The expansion is even', 'It does not expand', 'A'),
(6998, 8, 'How much joules of heat are given out when a piece of iron, of mass 60g and specific heat capacity 460Jkg-1K-1, cools from 75°C to 35°C', '1000J', '1050J', '1067J', '1104J', 'D'),
(6999, 8, 'The energy of light of frequency 2.0 x 10^15 Hz is (h = 6.63 x 10^-34 Js)', '3.33 x 10^-18 J', '1.33 x 10^-18 J', '1.33 x 10^-19 J', '3.33 x 10^-19 J', 'B'),
(7000, 8, 'A mass of gas at 40mmHg is heated from 298K to 348K at constant volume. Calculate the pressure exerted by the gas.', '50.21mmHg', '46.71mmHg', '42.35mmHg', '35.12mmHg', 'B'),
(7001, 8, 'The distance between two successive crests of a water wave is 0.25m. If a particle on the surface of the water makes four complete vertical oscillations in one second. Calculate the speed', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(7002, 8, 'The thermometer whose thermometric property is change in volume with temperature is', 'Resistance thermometer', 'Thermocouple', 'Bimetallic thermometer', 'Liquid-in-glass thermometer', 'D'),
(7003, 8, 'In a series resonant circuit, the current flowing in the circuit is', 'maximum', 'minimum', 'zero', 'unaffected', 'A'),
(7004, 8, 'If a body in linear motion changes from point P to Q, the motion is', 'Translational', 'Rotational', 'Simple harmonic', 'Circular', 'A'),
(7005, 8, 'Which of these gas laws is equivalent to workdone', 'Charle\'s law', 'Pressure law', 'Boyle\'s law', 'Gay Lussac\'s law', 'C');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `subjectyear_id`, `question`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `correct_option`) VALUES
(7006, 8, 'The process of adding impurities to a semiconductor material to increase its conductivity is', 'Rectification', 'Emission', 'Doping', 'Stabilization', 'C'),
(7007, 8, 'A load of 300N is to be lifted by a machine with a velocity ratio of 2 and an efficiency of 60% What effort will be applied to lift the load?', '100N', '150N', '250N', '400N', 'C'),
(7008, 8, 'The average translational kinetic energy of gas molecules depends on', 'Temperature only', 'Number of moles and temperature', 'Pressure and temperature', 'Pressure only', 'A'),
(7009, 8, 'The fourth overtone of a closed pipes is 900Hz, its fundamental frequency is', '50Hz', '100Hz', '200Hz', '400Hz', 'C'),
(7010, 8, 'A cell of internal resistance of 2 Ω supplies current through a resistor, X if the efficiency of the cell is 75%, find the value of X.', '2Ω', '4Ω', '6Ω', '8Ω', 'C'),
(7011, 8, 'Which of the following is the best as shaving mirror?', 'Concave mirror', 'Convex mirror', 'plane mirror', 'parabolic mirror', 'A'),
(7012, 8, 'A refrigerator uses 150w. If it is kept on for 336 hours non-stop, what is the energy consumed in KWh?', '60.20KWh', '50.40KWh', '25.01KWh', '30.20KWh', 'B'),
(7013, 8, 'What is the inductance reactance of a coil of 7H when connected to a 50Hz a.c circuit?', '2200Ω', '2000Ω', '1200Ω', '1100Ω', 'A'),
(7014, 8, 'If a charge ion goes through a combined electric field E and magnetic field B, the resultant emergent velocity of the ion is', 'E', 'EB', 'B', 'E/B', 'D'),
(7015, 8, 'In electrolysis, when same quantity of electricity is passed through different electrolytes, mass of substances deposited is proportional to', 'Molecular weight', 'Chemical equivalent', 'Atomic number', 'Chemical equivalent per valency', 'B'),
(7016, 8, 'If the rate of evaporation is y, and the rate of condensation is x, then, a vapour is saturated when', 'x > y', 'x < y', 'x = y', 'x ≤ y', 'C'),
(7017, 8, 'The degree of precision of a vernier caliper is', '0.005cm', '0.01cm', '0.1cm', '1.0cm', 'B'),
(7018, 8, 'According to kinetic theory of gases, the pressure exerted by the gas on the wall is equal', 'change in momentum per unit volume', 'rate of change of momentum imparted by the walls per second per unit area', 'momentum imparted to the walls per unit area', 'change in momentum imparted to the walls per unit area', 'B'),
(7019, 8, 'The property by which a material returns to its original shape after the removal of force is called', 'Elasticity', 'Ductility', 'Malleability', 'Plasticity', 'A'),
(7020, 8, 'The energy in a moving car is an example of', 'Mechanical energy', 'Electrical energy', 'Potential energy', 'Kinetic energy', 'D'),
(7021, 22, 'The vacuum and silvered wall surfaces of a vacuum flask walls are respectively', 'minimize conduction and convection and prevent radiation', 'prevent conduction and convection and minimize radiation', 'prevent conduction and minimize convection and radiation', 'minimize convection and prevent conduction and radiation', 'B'),
(7022, 22, 'The magnitude of the acceleration of a moving object is equal to the', 'gradient of a displacement-time graph', 'gradient of a velocity-time graph', 'area below a force-time graph', 'area below a velocity-time graph', 'B'),
(7023, 22, 'In which of the following states is MAXIMUM pressure exerted on a person', 'Standing on two feet', 'Standing on one foot', 'Lying on the floor', 'Kneeling on the floor', 'D'),
(7024, 22, 'What are cathode rays?', 'Stream of electrons', 'Beam of neutrons', 'Beam of protons', 'Stream of alpha particles', 'A'),
(7025, 22, 'The capacitance of a parallel plate capacitor', 'decreases when the temperature between the plates decreases', 'increases when the potential difference between the plates is increased', 'is greater without a dielectric between the plates than with dielectric', 'is greater with dielectric between the plates than without dielectric.', 'D'),
(7026, 22, 'The diagram above illustrates the motion of a cyclist from P to R. The distance travelled is determined by the', 'area under QR', 'area under PQR', 'gradient of PQR', 'gradient of QR', 'B'),
(7027, 22, 'A ray of light travels from a less dense medium to a denser medium. How are the speed and frequency of the light affected? The speed', 'Increases and the frequency increases', 'decreases and the frequency decreases', 'increases and the frequency remains the same', 'decreases and the frequency remains the same', 'D'),
(7028, 22, 'The function of a fuse in an electric circuit is to', 'break the circuit when the current exceeds a certain value', 'save energy by reducing voltage', 'ensure that the current in the circuit exceeds a certain value', 'save energy by reducing the current', 'A'),
(7029, 22, 'A body moves with uniform velocity when the resultant force on it is', 'greater than the frictional force acting on it', 'less than the frictional force acting on it', 'equal to zero', 'equal to unity', 'C'),
(7030, 22, 'The law of conservation of momentum is stated for closed and isolated system. What are the two conditions for a system to be closed and isolated?', 'No external force acts on the system and there is no change in mass of the system.', 'No external force acts on the system and there is a gain in mass.', 'No external force acts on the system and there is a loss in mass.', 'An external force acts on the system and there is no change in mass.', 'A'),
(7031, 22, 'A stone of mass 200g attached to a string is made to revolve in a horizontal circle of radius 1.5 m at a steady speed of 5 m/s. Calculate the tension in the string at the bottom of the circle.', '5.3N', '3.3N', '2.0N', '1.3N', 'B'),
(7032, 22, 'To convert a milli-ammeter to an ammeter, a resistor of low value is necessary to connect a resistor of', 'low value in series with it', 'high value in series with it', 'low value in parallel with it', 'high value in parallel with it', 'C'),
(7033, 22, 'An object is placed 1.5 m from a plane mirror. How far is the image from the object?', '3.0 m', '1.3 m', '1.0 m', '0.3 m', 'A'),
(7034, 22, 'Chromatic aberration in lenses can be corrected by using a combination of', 'diverging and converging lenses.', 'an opaque material to cover the rims of lenses.', 'wide parallel beams on the lenses\' surface.', 'a thin convex lens.', 'A'),
(7035, 22, 'A cube of wood with side 10.0cm floats vertically in water with 4.5cm of its length submerged. Calculate the density of the wood. [Density of water = 1g/cm³]', '0.090g/cm³', '0.450g/cm³', '0.230g/cm³', '0.0450g/cm³', 'B'),
(7036, 22, 'A temperature of 60°C is equivalent to', '25°F', '140°F', '50°F', '108°F', 'B'),
(7037, 22, 'All of the following uses are practical applications of x-ray except', 'the treatment of tumors', 'determining the depth of a mine', 'dental operation', 'detecting fractures in bones', 'B'),
(7038, 22, 'Two isolated charged spheres each of magnitude +1.0×10⁻⁶ C are separated by a distance of 2.0×10⁻¹ m. Calculate the magnitude of the electrostatic force between them [K = 1/4πε₀ = 9×10⁹ Nm²C⁻²]', '2.25×10⁻¹ N', '4.50×10⁻¹ N', '2.25×10¹ N', '4.50×10¹ N', 'A'),
(7039, 22, 'In the circuit diagram above, which lamp causes the other to go off?', 'P', 'Q', 'R', 'S', 'B'),
(7040, 22, 'A particle of mass 3.6 × 10⁻⁶ kg revolving around the earth has a radial acceleration of 4.3 × 10⁷ ms⁻². Calculate the centripetal force of the particle.', '1.55 × 10² N', '2.00 × 10⁻² N', '6.25 × 10⁻¹⁴ N', '1.00 × 10² N', 'A'),
(7041, 22, 'For a convex lens to form a real image, the distance between the object and the screen will be:', 'equal to the focal length of the lens', 'less than the focal length of the lens', 'twice the focal length of the lens', 'four times the focal length of the lens', 'D'),
(7042, 22, 'A constant voltage source supplies a sinusoidal alternating e.m.f. The voltage marked against the components are their peak values. Determine the peak value of the applied e.m.f', '1V', '4V', '5V', '2V', 'C'),
(7043, 22, 'A 2 μF capacitor is connected directly across a 150 Vrms, 60 Hz A.C source. Calculate the rms value of the current.', '0.113A', '0.160A', '150A', '1324A', 'A'),
(7044, 22, 'A body of mass, m is projected vertically upward with a velocity, v. At what position will the potential energy be maximum?', 'v/g', '2v²/g', 'v²/2g', 'v²/4g', 'C'),
(7045, 22, 'Light of energy 1.12×10⁻¹⁸ J is incident on a metal. The ejected electrons have maximum energy of 8.0×10⁻¹⁹ J. Calculate the threshold frequency of the metal. [h = 6.626×10⁻³⁴ Js]', '4.8×10¹⁴ Hz', '1.2×10¹⁵ Hz', '1.7×10¹⁵ Hz', '2.8×10¹⁵ Hz', 'A'),
(7046, 22, 'An object 2.0cm high is placed at the radius of curvature of a concave mirror such that it is perpendicular to the principal axis of the mirror. Determine the height of the image.', '0.5 cm', '1.0 cm', '1.5 cm', '2.0 cm', 'D'),
(7047, 22, 'The diagram above illustrates two boxes P and Q of masses 27.3 kg and 6.2 kg respectively on a smooth horizontal surface. If a force F of 150 N is applied to the combined masses, calculate the acceleration.', '4.5 ms⁻²', '33.5 ms⁻²', '70 ms⁻²', '150 ms⁻²', 'A'),
(7048, 22, 'A boy of mass 40 kg jumps off a stationary skateboard and moves horizontally with a speed of 1.5 m/s while the skateboard moves in the opposite direction with a speed of 20 m/s. Calculate the mass of the skateboard.', '60 kg', '40 kg', '3 kg', '2 kg', 'C'),
(7049, 22, 'The depolarizing agent in a Leclanché cell is', 'powdered carbon.', 'manganese (IV) oxide.', 'carbon rod.', 'ammonium.', 'B'),
(7050, 22, 'Which of the following terms has different dimension from the others?', 'Stress × Strain', 'Pressure', 'Stress/Strain', 'Torque', 'D'),
(7051, 22, 'A capacitor described as a mica capacitor has', 'both plates are made of mica.', 'a mica dielectric.', 'a dielectric made of mica', 'the same capacitance as that of mica', 'C'),
(7052, 22, 'In which of the following devices is the thermal expansion considered a disadvantage?', 'Fire alarm', 'Thermostat', 'Bimetallic thermometer', 'Balance wheel of a watch', 'D'),
(7053, 22, 'The inside portion of a hollow metal sphere of diameter 20cm is polished. The portion will therefore form a', 'Concave mirror of focal length 5cm.', 'Concave mirror of focal length 10 cm.', 'Convex mirror of focal length 10 cm', 'Convex mirror of focal length 5cm', 'A'),
(7054, 22, 'Which of the following statements about a projectile is not correct?', 'Projectile motion is a two-dimensional motion.', 'A projectile is an object launched into the air and allowed to move freely due to gravity.', 'The range of a projectile is independent of the acceleration due to gravity.', 'The time of flight is dependent on the acceleration due to gravity', 'C'),
(7055, 22, 'Atmospheric pressure decreases with an increase in altitude because:', 'Acceleration due to gravity increases with altitude.', 'Temperature increases with altitude.', 'Internal energy increases with altitude.', 'Interaction among air molecules decreases due to less quantity of air.', 'D'),
(7056, 22, 'The main difference between X-rays and gamma rays is in their', 'ionizing ability.', 'absorbing rate.', 'mode of propagation.', 'mode of production.', 'D'),
(7057, 22, 'The phenomenon used for explaining the formation of a rainbow in the sky is', 'interference.', 'refraction.', 'reflection.', 'dispersion.', 'D'),
(7058, 22, 'Which of the following modes is the most economical method of transmitting electrical power over a long distance?', 'Alternating current at high voltage and low current.', 'Alternating current at low voltage and high current.', 'Direct current at high voltage and low current.', 'Direct current at low voltage and high current.', 'A'),
(7059, 22, 'The correct sequence of ionization power of alpha particle, gamma ray, and beta particle respectively is', 'low, medium, high.', 'high, medium, low.', 'medium, low, high.', 'high, low, medium.', 'D'),
(7060, 22, 'Four pieces of constantan wire, marked E, F, G, and H, each of length 1.0m, are at the same temperature. Their respective diameters are 1mm, 2mm, 6mm, and 10mm. Which wire has the highest resistance?', 'E', 'F', 'G', 'H', 'A'),
(7061, 22, 'The maximum displacement of particles from equilibrium position in a wave motion is known as', 'wave length.', 'amplitude.', 'frequency.', 'polarization.', 'B'),
(7062, 22, 'A non-conducting vessel contains a liquid of mass 70g at 25°C. Another 70.0g of the same liquid at 35°C is quickly poured into the vessel. Determine the final temperature of the mixture', '15°C', '20°C', '30°C', '40°C', 'C'),
(7063, 22, 'A galvanometer of full-scale deflection 10 mA has a resistance of 5Ω. Calculate the shunt needed to convert it to measure currents of 2 A.', '0.025Ω', '0.050Ω', '0.250Ω', '0.500Ω', 'A'),
(7064, 22, 'In storing magnets, the keeper is used to', 'cancel the effect of the earth\'s magnetism', 'reduce self demagnetization', 'protect the magnet from stray electric field', 'increase the strength of the magnet.', 'B'),
(7065, 22, 'Which of the following factors does not affect the speed of sound?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(7066, 22, 'A convex mirror is used as a driving mirror; however, a disadvantage in this regard is that the image', 'it produces is virtual.', 'it produces is real.', 'is not as bright as we would like', 'appears farther away from the driver', 'D'),
(7067, 22, 'The amount of heat energy that will be extracted when 0.02kg of water vapor condenses to water at 97°C is [specific heat capacity of water = 4200 Jkg⁻¹K⁻¹, specific latent heat of vaporization of water = 2.26×10⁶ Jkg⁻¹]', '45,452J', '45,200J', '25,200J', '252J', 'A'),
(7068, 22, 'Water is readily available but it is not a good thermometric liquid mainly because it', 'clings to glass', 'does not expand uniformly', 'boils at low temperature', 'is colourless', 'B'),
(7069, 22, 'The constant temperature at which a liquid changes into gaseous state is known as', 'evaporation point', 'boiling point', 'melting point', 'dew point', 'B'),
(7070, 22, 'The diagram above illustrates the graph for', 'the variation of the volume of a gas with increasing temperature', 'expansion curve of mercury', 'expansion curve of liquid oxygen', 'anomalous expansion of water', 'D'),
(7071, 35, 'Evaluate and correct to two decimal places: 75.0785 - 34.624 + 9.83.', '30.60', '50.29', '50.28', '30.63', 'B'),
(7072, 35, 'If X = {x: x < 7} and Y = {y: y is a factor of 24} are subsets of μ = {1,2,3...10}, find X ∩ Y', '{2,3,4,6}', '{1,2,3,4,6}', '{2,3,4,6,8}', '{1,2,3,4,6,8}', 'B'),
(7073, 35, 'Simplify [(16/9)^(-3/2) × 16^(-3/2)]^(1/3)', '3/4', '9/16', '3/8', '1/4', 'C'),
(7074, 35, 'Express 1 + 2log₁₀3 in the form of log₁₀x', 'log₁₀90', 'log₁₀19', 'log₁₀9', 'log₁₀6', 'A'),
(7075, 35, 'If 101₂ + 21ᵧ = 33₅, find the value of y', '8', '7', '6', '5', 'C'),
(7076, 35, 'An amount of ₦550,000.00 was realized when a principal, x was saved at 2% simple interest for 5 years. Find the value of x.', '₦470,000.00', '₦480,000.00', '₦490,000.00', '₦500,000.00', 'D'),
(7077, 35, 'Given that (√3 + √5)/√5 = x + y√15, find the value of (x + y)', '1 3/5', '1 2/5', '1 1/5', '1/5', 'C'),
(7078, 35, 'If x = 3 and y = -1, evaluate 2(x² - y³)', '24', '22', '20', '16', 'D'),
(7079, 35, 'Solve 3x - 2y = 10 and x + 3y = 7 simultaneously.', 'x = -4 and y = 1', 'x = -1 and y = -4', 'x = 1 and y = 4', 'x = 4 and y = 1', 'D'),
(7080, 35, 'The implication x → y is equivalent to?', '~y → ~x', 'y → ~x', '~x → ~y', 'y → x', 'A'),
(7081, 35, 'The first term of a geometric progression is 3 and the 5th term is 48. Find the common ratio.', '2', '4', '8', '16', 'A'),
(7082, 35, 'Solve 1/3 (5 - 3x) < 2/5 (3 - 7x)', 'x > 7/22', 'x < 7/22', 'x > -7/27', 'x < -7/27', 'C'),
(7083, 35, 'Make m the subject of the relation k = √[(m - y)/(m + 1)]', 'm = (y + k²)/(k² + 1)', 'm = (y + k²)/(1 - k²)', 'm = (y - k²)/(k² + 1)', 'm = (y - k²)/(1 - k²)', 'B'),
(7084, 35, 'Find the quadratic equation whose roots are 1/2 and -1/3.', '3x² + x + 1 = 0', '6x² + x - 1 = 0', '3x² + x - 1 = 0', '6x² - x - 1 = 0', 'D'),
(7085, 35, 'Given that x is directly proportional to y and inversely proportional to z, x = 15 when y = 10 and z = 4, find the equation connecting x, y and z.', 'x = 6y/z', 'x = 12y/z', 'x = 3y/z', 'x = 3y/(2z)', 'A'),
(7086, 35, 'Two buses start from the same station at 9.00 am and travel in opposite directions along the same straight road. The first bus travels at a speed of 72 km/h and the second at 48 km/h. At what time will they be 240 km apart?', '1:00 pm', '12:00 noon', '11:00 am', '10:00 am', 'C'),
(7087, 35, 'A solid cuboid has a length of 7 cm, a width of 5 cm, and a height of 4 cm. Calculate its total surface area.', '280 cm²', '166 cm²', '140 cm²', '83 cm²', 'B'),
(7088, 35, 'In the diagram, PQ || SR. Find the value of x.', '34', '46', '57', '68', 'B'),
(7089, 35, 'Find the equation of the line parallel to 2y = 3(x - 2) and passes through the point (2,3).', 'y = (2/3)x - 3', 'y = (2/3)x - 2', 'y = (3/2)x', 'y = -(2/3)x', 'C'),
(7090, 35, 'The expression (5x + 3)/[6x(x + 1)] will be undefined when x equals:', '{0,1}', '{0,-1}', '{-3,-11}', '{-3,0}', 'B'),
(7091, 35, 'A man is five times as old as his son. In four years time, the product of their ages would be 340. If the son\'s age is y, express the product of their ages in terms of y.', '5y² - 16y - 380 = 0', '5y² - 24y - 380 = 0', '5y² - 16y - 330 = 0', '5y² + 24y - 324 = 0', 'D'),
(7092, 35, 'Simplify a/b - b/a - c/b', '(a - b + c)/(ab)', '(ab - bc - ac)/(ab)', '(a² - b² + ac)/(ab)', '(a² - b² - ac)/(ab)', 'D'),
(7093, 35, 'In the diagram, XYZ is an equilateral triangle of side 6 cm and Y is the midpoint of XY. Find tan(∠XZT).', '1/√3', '√3/2', '√3', '1/2', 'A'),
(7094, 35, 'A fence 2.4 m tall is 10 m away from a tree of height 16 m. Calculate the angle of elevation of the top of the tree from the top of the fence.', '76.11°', '53.67°', '52.40°', '51.32°', 'D'),
(7095, 35, 'Fati buys milk at ₦x per tin and sells each at a profit of ₦y. If she sells 10 tins of milk, how much does she receive from the sales?', '₦(xy + 10)', '₦(x + 10y)', '₦(10x + y)', '₦10(x + y)', 'D'),
(7096, 35, 'If tan y is positive and sin y is negative, in which quadrant would y lie?', 'First and third only', 'First and second only', 'Third only', 'Second only', 'C'),
(7097, 35, 'The dimension of a rectangular base of a right pyramid is 9 cm by 5 cm. If the volume of the pyramid is 105 cm³, how high is the pyramid?', '10 cm', '6 cm', '8 cm', '7 cm', 'D'),
(7098, 35, 'Each interior angle of a regular polygon is 168°. Find the number of sides of the polygon.', '30', '36', '24', '18', 'A'),
(7099, 35, 'In the diagram, MN || PQ, ∠MNP = 2x and ∠MNP = (3x - 50)°. Find the value of ∠MNP.', '200°', '100°', '120°', '90°', 'B'),
(7100, 35, 'The length of an arc of a circle of radius 3.5 cm is 19/36 cm. Calculate, correct to the nearest degree, the angle subtended at the centre of the circle. [Take π = 22/7]', '55°', '36°', '25°', '22°', 'D'),
(7101, 35, 'In the diagram, PU || SR, PS || TR, QS || UR, |UR| = 15 cm, |SR| = 8 cm, |PS| = 10 cm and the area of triangle SUR is 24 cm². Calculate the area of PTRS.', '40 cm²', '48 cm²', '80 cm²', '120 cm²', 'C'),
(7102, 35, 'In the diagram, there is a circle with center O. If ∠OPQ = 48°, find the value of m.', '96°', '90°', '68°', '42°', 'D'),
(7103, 35, 'The pie chart shows the population of men, women, and children in a city. If the population of the city is 1,800,000, how many men are in the city?', '845,000', '600,000', '355,000', '250,000', 'C'),
(7104, 35, 'The mean of the numbers 15, 21, 17, 26, 18 and 29 is 21. Calculate the standard deviation.', '9', '6', '5', '0', 'C'),
(7105, 35, 'Find the sum of the interior angles of a pentagon.', '340°', '350°', '540°', '550°', 'C'),
(7106, 35, 'Calculate, correct to the nearest cm³, the volume of a sphere of radius 6 cm. [Take π = 22/7]', '903 cm³', '904 cm³', '905 cm³', '906 cm³', 'C'),
(7107, 35, 'A box contains 12 identical balls of which 5 are red, 4 blue, and the rest are green. If a ball is selected at random from the box, what is the probability that it is green?', '3/4', '1/2', '1/3', '1/4', 'D'),
(7108, 35, 'A box contains 12 identical balls of which 5 are red, 4 blue, and the rest are green. If two balls are selected at random one after the other with replacement, what is the probability that both are red?', '25/144', '5/33', '5/6', '103/132', 'A'),
(7109, 35, 'In the diagram, PQ is a straight line. If m = ½(x + y + z), find the value of m.', '45°', '60°', '90°', '100°', 'C'),
(7110, 35, 'The points on a linear graph are as shown in the table: x: 6.20, 6.85, 7.50; y: 3.90, 5.20, 6.50. Find the gradient (slope) of the line.', '2½', '2', '1', '½', 'B'),
(7111, 35, 'In the diagram, O is the center of the circle. PQ and RS are tangents to the circle. Find the value of (m + n)°.', '120°', '90°', '75°', '60°', 'D'),
(7112, 35, 'Which of the following is not a sufficient condition for two triangles to be congruent?', 'AAS', 'SSS', 'SAS', 'SSA', 'D'),
