(8082, 69, 'The following can be used to improve a country\'s balance of payment EXCEPT', 'Anti-dumping policies', 'Granting subsidies to export producers', 'Decreasing taxation on personal income', 'Increasing import duties', 'C'),
(8083, 69, 'In the equation Q = a - bP + e; Q and P are _____ variables respectively.', 'Independent and dependent', 'Dependent and independent', 'Independent and constant', 'Error term and independent', 'B'),
(8084, 69, 'Which of the following is NOT an objective of Economic planning?', 'Equitable allocation of resources', 'Widening the income gap', 'Achieving economic growth', 'Creating employment', 'B'),
(8085, 69, 'The following determine the level of consumption EXCEPT', 'Level of income', 'The rate of taxes paid', 'Savings', 'The political climate', 'D'),
(8086, 69, 'The following are problems of development planning in Nigeria EXCEPT', 'Inadequate capital', 'Under-population', 'Inadequate statistical data', 'Poor implementation of economic planning', 'B'),
(8087, 69, 'The system of farming which involves the use of a large hectare of land planted with economic crops is known as', 'Peasant farming', 'Tree planting', 'Plantation farming', 'Mechanized farming', 'C'),
(8088, 69, 'At the equilibrium price,', 'Demand equates supply', 'Price is equal to demand only', 'Demand is less than supply', 'Demand is greater than supply', 'A'),
(8089, 69, 'Which of the following is a disadvantage of localization of industries?', 'Creating structural unemployment', 'Reducing cost of production', 'Encouraging the growth of skilled labour', 'Encouraging subsidiary industries', 'A'),
(8090, 69, 'Stock exchange market deals with', 'Sales of second hand securities', 'Sales of foreign exchange', 'Exchange of stock fish for stock', 'Exchange of treasury bills', 'A'),
(8091, 69, 'Which of the following is NOT a major role of OPEC in production and marketing of petroleum?', 'Stabilizing oil prices by putting a production ceiling', 'Refining of petroleum products in member countries', 'Raising the revenue of member countries from oil through price increase', 'Ensuring efficient and regular supply of oil to the world market', 'B'),
(8092, 69, 'The satisfaction derived from the consumption of a commodity is referred to as', 'Consumption', 'Production', 'Utility', 'Demand', 'C'),
(8093, 69, 'An industry engaged in the extraction of raw materials and its conversion into semi-finished goods is called ______ industry.', 'Mining', 'Manufacturing', 'Processing', 'Conversion', 'C'),
(8094, 69, 'An industry operating in a perfect competitive market situation will maximize profit when', 'DD < SS', 'MC > AC', 'MC = MR', 'MC < AR', 'C'),
(8095, 52, 'Which of the following is an example of a microorganism in action as a disease vector?', 'Fungi decomposing dead plant material', 'Mosquito transmitting malaria', 'Bacteria causing food poisoning', 'Algae producing oxygen through photosynthesis', 'B'),
(8096, 52, 'Which of the following is a characteristic of cells related to irritability?', 'Ability to respond to stimuli', 'Ability to synthesize proteins', 'Ability to generate energy', 'Ability to replicate DNA', 'A'),
(8097, 52, 'The membrane around the vacuole is known as', 'Elaioplast', 'Amyloplast', 'Tonoplast', 'Cytoplast', 'C'),
(8098, 52, 'Which of the following is evidence of evolution?', 'All of the above', 'Similarities in embryonic development', 'Fossils of extinct organisms', 'Homologous structures in different species', 'A'),
(8099, 52, 'Which of the following is an example of an adaptation for survival in social insects?', 'Migration to warmer climates', 'Production of venom for defense', 'Formation of complex caste systems', 'Hibernation during winter months', 'C'),
(8100, 52, 'Which of the following is NOT a part of the alimentary canal?', 'Oesophagus', 'Large intestine', 'Liver', 'Small intestine', 'C'),
(8101, 52, 'Which of the following is an evolutionary trend commonly observed in organisms?', 'Decreased complexity over time', 'Increased dependence on external resources', 'Increased genetic diversity within populations', 'Decreased adaptation to the environment', 'C'),
(8102, 52, 'Which of the following is a characteristic feature of Kingdom Plantae?', 'Presence of chloroplasts', 'Ability to perform photosynthesis', 'Lack of cell walls', 'Heterotrophic mode of nutrition', 'B'),
(8103, 52, 'A biome characterized by hot summer, warm winter and treeless vegetation is', 'Steppe grasslands', 'Temperate deserts', 'Savannah grassland', 'Tropical deserts', 'A'),
(8104, 52, 'Which of the following is an example of physiological variation in organisms?', 'Variation in blood pressure among individuals', 'Variation in beak shape among finches', 'Differences in fur color in rabbits', 'Variation in leaf shape in plants', 'A'),
(8105, 52, 'Which of the following are components of the skeletal system in humans?', 'Cartilage and blood vessels', 'Ligaments and tendons', 'Muscles and nerves', 'Bones and joints', 'D'),
(8106, 52, 'Which of the following represents an example of ecological management and conservation through a biological association?', 'Construction of a dam for hydroelectric power', 'Introduction of an invasive species for pest control', 'Clear-cutting of a forest for timber extraction', 'Establishment of marine protected areas', 'D'),
(8107, 52, 'The term cell was given by', 'Robert Hooke', 'Schwann', 'De Bary', 'Tatum', 'A'),
(8108, 52, 'Which of the following is the primary organ involved in gas exchange during respiration in humans?', 'Diaphragm', 'Bronchi', 'Lungs', 'Trachea', 'C'),
(8109, 52, 'Which gland is responsible for producing the hormone insulin?', 'Thyroid gland', 'Pituitary gland', 'Pancreas', 'Adrenal gland', 'C'),
(8110, 52, 'Most fishes do not sink in water because of the presence of: I. swim bladder II. air bladder III. air sacs IV. air in spongy bones', 'II and III are correct', 'I and II are correct', 'I, II, III and IV are correct', 'III and IV are correct', 'B'),
(8111, 52, 'In monohybrid inheritance, if an organism carries two different alleles for a particular gene, it is called:', 'Homozygous', 'Dominant', 'Heterozygous', 'Recessive', 'C'),
(8112, 52, 'What is the tissue responsible for transporting water and minerals from the roots to the rest of the plant?', 'Xylem', 'Epidermis', 'Parenchyma', 'Phloem', 'A'),
