(8561, 58, 'The climatic belts recognized by the Greek were', 'Hot, mild and cool', 'Equatorial, polar and torrid', 'Torrid, temperate and frigid', 'Hot, cold and medium', 'C'),
(8562, 58, 'A conurbation can best be described as', 'Two or more towns joined together, each town maintaining its own identity', 'A big area of land with few settlements', 'A large village with thousands of people', 'A large area with big cities', 'A'),
(8563, 58, 'Sills, dykes and batholiths are examples of', 'Extrusive volcanic landforms', 'Depositional landforms', 'Intrusive volcanic landforms', 'Landforms from earthquakes', 'C'),
(8564, 58, 'Which of the following is not true of pie chart?', 'Data with wide extreme can be conveniently represented in a pie chart', 'Statistics of various item can be represented on a single diagram', 'It is often difficult to compare the component parts', 'It is easy to draw', 'A'),
(8565, 58, 'Which of the following environmental hazards is due primarily to human activities?', 'Hurricane', 'Ozone depletion', 'Earthquake', 'Volcanic eruption', 'B'),
(8566, 58, 'Life expectancy refers to the', 'Age at which people retire from their jobs', 'Average age at which people die', 'Age at which people receive their pension', 'Achievement one makes in life', 'B'),
(8567, 58, 'The most common mode of transportation in Africa is', 'Road', 'Rail', 'Ocean', 'Air', 'A'),
(8568, 58, 'A great advantage of Basin irrigation is that', 'The basin helps to trap much alluvium to enrich the soil', 'It makes it possible to irrigate larger areas', 'It is an expensive means of irrigation', 'Water is not wasted', 'A'),
(8569, 58, 'All the following are problems of mining in Africa except', 'Inadequate unskilled labour', 'Use of obsolete technology', 'Shortage of power', 'Inadequate foreign capital', 'A'),
(8570, 58, 'A settlement developed at the meeting point of roads is known as a', 'Port town', 'Nodal town', 'Confluence town', 'Gap town', 'B'),
(8571, 58, 'Africa\'s largest timber producer is', 'Ghana', 'Malawi', 'Zaire', 'Nigeria', 'A'),
(8572, 58, 'A geyser is best described as', 'Explosion of volcano', 'Fountain of super heated steam', 'Thermal stream', 'Pool of hot water', 'B'),
(8573, 58, 'Which of the following is not correct about the great circle?', 'The Equator is a Great Circle among the latitudes', 'The Greenwich Meridian and the International Date Line are the only lines of longitude forming a Great Circle', 'The Great Circle divides the earth into two equal spheres', 'The centre of the Great Circle is also the centre of the earth', 'B'),
(8574, 58, 'The main reason for which most manufacturing industries in West Africa are concentrated in cities and towns along the coast is that they have', 'A large number of warehouses', 'Large urban market', 'A large pool of unskilled labour', 'Numerous banks', 'B'),
(8575, 58, 'The type of agriculture in which water is conserved in a year so that crops can be grown in succeeding years by ploughing, mulching or harrowing is known as', 'Arable farming', 'Intensive cultivation', 'Extensive cultivation', 'Dry farming', 'D'),
(8576, 58, 'Which of the following sources of power supply is renewable?', 'Gas', 'Nuclear', 'Solar', 'Coal', 'C'),
(8577, 57, 'An instruction of thick acid lava, which forces overlaying sedimentary rock layers to bulge into a dome, may cool and solidify to form a', 'Batholith', 'Laccolith', 'Dyke', 'Lopolith', 'B'),
(8578, 57, 'The Greek system of classifying climate is based on', 'Temperature', 'Rainfall and temperature', 'Rainfall and vegetation', 'Humidity', 'A'),
(8579, 57, 'What will be the time at Greenwich meridian when it is 12 noon at longitude 60°E?', '4.00 a.m.', '4.00 p.m', '8.00 a.m.', '8.00 p.m.', 'C'),
(8580, 57, 'The movement of Earth around the sun on its elliptical orbit is called', 'Rotation', 'Axis', 'Revolution', 'Gravitation', 'C'),
(8581, 57, 'The Deccan Plateau in India is a good example of', 'Dissected plateau', 'Volcanic plateau', 'Tectonic plateau', 'Intermontane plateau', 'B'),
(8582, 57, 'Horst is a feature associated with?', 'Volcanic mountain', 'Residual mountain', 'Block mountain', 'Fold mountain', 'C'),
(8583, 57, 'Which of the following pairs of land forms are surface features of a karst region? i. Clint ii. Grikes iii. Stalagmite iv. Cavin', 'i and ii only', 'i and iii only', 'ii and iii only', 'ii and iv only', 'A'),
(8584, 57, 'Two towns, A and B, are on the international dateline. What will be the distance between the two towns if town A is located on latitude 40°N and town B is located on latitude 10°N?', '8880 kilometers', '5550 kilometers', '3330 kilometers', '2220 kilometers', 'C'),
(8585, 57, 'Wind erosion results in the formation of the following land forms except.', 'Zeugen', 'Yardang', 'Ventifact', 'Barchan', 'D'),
(8586, 57, 'Which of the following best explains the breaking down of well jointed rocks into large rectangular-shaped features by mechanical weathering?', 'Block disintegration', 'Exfoliation dome', 'Landslide', 'Solifluction', 'A'),
(8587, 57, 'Which of the following sequence is correct in the formation of a stack?', 'Cave, arch, headland, stack', 'Headland, cave, arch, stack', 'Headland, arch, cave, stack', 'Cave, headland, arch, stack', 'B'),
(8588, 57, 'Which of the following conditions can produce a waterfall?', 'Sharp break in the bed of a river', 'Elbow of capture of young rivers', 'Backward erosion', 'Lateral erosion', 'A'),
(8589, 57, 'In which of the following regions will weathering by frost action occur throughout the years?', 'Cool temperate', 'Equatorial', 'Monsoon', 'Mediterranean', 'A'),
(8590, 57, 'The lapse rate refers to the average rate at which ?', 'Radiant energy is converted to heat', 'Air pressure decreases with altitude', 'Air pressure increases with altitude', 'Temperature decreases with altitude', 'D'),
(8591, 57, 'Which of the following is proof of the Earth\'s spherical shape?', 'Circumnavigation', 'Variation in the length of the day and night making of a year', 'Rise and fall of tides', 'The sun rises in the east and sets in the west', 'A'),
(8592, 57, 'Which of the following types of rocks contain fossils?', 'Igneous', 'Sedimentary', 'Metamorphic', 'Volcanic', 'B');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `subjectyear_id`, `question`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `correct_option`) VALUES
(8593, 57, 'The natural exchange of water between land, oceans and the atmosphere is known as', 'Energy cycle', 'Hydrological cycle', 'Nitrogen cycle', 'Carbon cycle', 'B'),
(8594, 57, 'Lines drawn on a map connecting places with equal duration of sunshine are called', 'Isohels', 'Isotherms', 'Isonephs', 'Isohyets', 'A'),
(8595, 57, 'Which of the following examples of rock is mostly likely to be weathered by the process of solution ?', 'Slates', 'Graphite', 'Limestone', 'Granite', 'C'),
(8596, 57, 'Which of the following occurs when the sun is vertically overhead at the equator?', 'Equinox', 'Solstice', 'Deflection of winds and ocean currents', 'Rise and fall of tides', 'A'),
(8597, 57, 'Which of the following pairs of ways can be used to solve the world\'s high population concentration problems? i. family planning ii. sex education iii. early marriage iv. industrialization', 'i and ii only', 'ii and iii only', 'iii and iv only', 'i and iv only', 'A'),
(8598, 57, 'Which of the following countries in West Africa is well known for the production of diamonds?', 'Togo', 'Burkina Faso', 'Sierra Leone', 'Benin', 'C'),
(8599, 57, 'Which of the following is a leading industrial area in North America?', 'The northeastern industrial area of USA', 'Central Canada industrial area', 'South Mexico Industrial Area', 'The Guatemala industrial area', 'A'),
(8600, 57, '\"It is an intensive cultivation of fruits, vegetables, flowers, it is small-scale farming, the yields are very high per hectare, produce sold to customers is usually fresh, and commonly practiced in urban communities.\" The above statements are the characteristics of a?', 'Mixed farming', 'Sericulture', 'Market gardening', 'Viniculture', 'C'),
(8601, 57, 'An advantage of a large population is?', 'Increase in government expenditure', 'Surplus empowerment opportunities', 'Abundant labour force', 'Small market for goods', 'C'),
(8602, 57, 'Which of the following best describes the relationship between rural and urban areas?', 'Urban areas are not as important as rural areas', 'Urban and rural areas depend on each other', 'Rural areas exist only to serve urban areas', 'Urban areas can exist without rural areas', 'B'),
(8603, 57, 'Which of the following factors has the greatest influence on the location of the cement industry?', 'Proximity to source of raw materials', 'Nearness to market', 'Source of capital', 'Manpower development', 'A'),
(8604, 57, 'Which of the following best describes high population growth?', 'The number of births equals the number of deaths', 'Birth rate are equal to death rate', 'Emigration is equal to immigration', 'Birth rates are higher than death rates', 'D'),
(8605, 57, 'Which of the following pairs of activities can initiate deforestation? i. lumbering ii. afforestation iii. excavation iv. grazing', 'i and iv only', 'ii and iii only', 'ii and iv only', 'i and ii only', 'A'),
(8606, 57, 'Which of the following is a major of plantation agriculture?', 'Control weeds with herbicide', 'Encourage monoculture', 'Foreign exchange earners', 'Application of modern technology', 'C'),
(8607, 57, 'Which of the following is arranged according to the increasing size of settlement?', 'Town, conurbation, hamlet, and village', 'Hamlet, village, town and conurbation', 'Village, town, conurbation, and hamlet', 'Conurbation, town, hamlet, and village', 'B'),
(8608, 57, 'Wood carving, leather work, and cloth weaving are examples of?', 'Chemical industry', 'Power industry', 'Heavy industry', 'Local craft industry', 'D'),
(8609, 57, 'Population density is defined as the average', 'Number of people in the capital town', 'Number of people living in a unit area', 'Number of human resources', 'Number of deaths and births in a unit area', 'B'),
(8610, 57, 'A settlement pattern in which houses are arranged along lines of transportation is described as', 'Dispersed', 'Linear', 'Radial', 'Nucleated', 'B');
